{"id":176,"title":"Helmor — Local Workbench for Multi-Agent Dev with Voice Copilot","url":"https://github.com/dohooo/helmor","category":"coding_agents","stars":1105,"added":"2026-05-22 04:05:59.61762+00","description":"Open-source local workbench for multi-agent dev. Uses gpt-realtime-2 for voice-controlled agent orchestration. All UI actions have CLI equivalents."}
{"id":178,"title":"ProgramBench — Can LLMs Rebuild Programs From Scratch?","url":"https://github.com/facebookresearch/ProgramBench","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":636,"added":"2026-05-22 04:40:53.664818+00","description":"From the SWE-Bench team (Princeton/Meta/Stanford). Gives models a compiled binary + docs, asks them to rebuild from scratch. 9 frontier models tested, zero fully resolved. Leading model passed 95%% tests on only 3%% of tasks. 200 tasks total."}
{"id":180,"title":"rmux — Universal Rust Multiplexer for Driving CLI/TUI Apps from Code","url":"https://github.com/Helvesec/rmux","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":1046,"added":"2026-05-22 05:06:15.504565+00","description":"Universal Rust multiplexer with typed SDK. Drive any CLI or TUI app from code. Native on Linux, macOS, Windows. Built with tokio and ratatui. 572 stars in 7 days."}
{"id":181,"title":"AI Kill Chain — Defender-Side Extension of Lockheed Martin Cyber Kill Chain for LLM/Agent Threats","url":"https://github.com/gouravnagar-infosec/ai-kill-chain","category":"agent_security","stars":37,"added":"2026-05-22 06:08:24.296161+00","description":"Extends the classic kill chain with a model supply chain stage and splits actions-on-objectives into exfiltration, model extraction, and agentic pivot stages. 37 stars but 33 forks — practitioners are actually using it."}
