{"id":264,"title":"Nebula Security Vega — AI Agent Discovered nginx-poolslip Zero-Day RCE","url":"https://x.com/nebusecurity/status/2057071579876753643","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 03:07:01.127626+00","description":"AI security agent Vega found an unauthenticated RCE zero-day in nginx 1.31.0. Targets nginx core memory pool management (ngx_pool_t). Exploit includes ASLR bypass via heap feng shui + address leaking. Achieves reverse shell. 452K views, 1383 likes, 252 RTs on disclosure. No CVE assigned yet. No public PoC. Responsible disclosure — full writeup released 30 days after patch."}
{"id":265,"title":"Agentics — GitHub Next Agentic Workflows for Autonomous Repo Maintenance (714 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/githubnext/agentics","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":714,"added":"2026-05-23 03:07:02.882145+00","description":"Sample pack of GitHub Agentic Workflows by GitHub Next. Includes repo-assist agent that reduced open issues by 578 across 13 repos, achieved 8x issue closure velocity and 10x PR merge speed. Transforms dormant open source projects into actively maintained ones. Official GitHub team project."}
{"id":266,"title":"GitNexus — Zero-Server Code Intelligence Engine for AI Agents (39.8K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":40012,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Client-side knowledge graph that indexes codebases into dependency/call-chain/execution-flow graphs. Exposes via MCP so Cursor, Claude Code, Codex get architectural context and stop shipping blind edits. Runs entirely in browser."}
{"id":267,"title":"Orca — Next-Gen ADE for Parallel Agent Fleets (3.1K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/stablyai/orca","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":3096,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Agent Development Environment that runs any coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Pi, Cursor) in parallel fleets with one subscription. Desktop and mobile apps."}
{"id":268,"title":"Sigil — AI Security Posture Management for Developer Machines","url":"https://github.com/Ju571nK/sigil","category":"agent_security","stars":2,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Host-side agent that watches files controlling what AI coding agents can do: hooks, permissions, MCP allowlists, sandbox flags. Scores dangerous configurations and ships events to SIEM. Rust. Monitors Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI."}
{"id":269,"title":"Adrian — Runtime Security Monitoring for AI Agents (71 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/secureagentics/Adrian","category":"agent_security","stars":71,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Catches malicious tool use, prompt injection, and policy drift in real-time. Runtime security layer for autonomous agents. Python."}
{"id":270,"title":"JanuScope — Local-First MCP Policy Proxy (15 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/giancarloerra/JanuScope","category":"agent_security","stars":15,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Tool-block, SQL-mutation gate, PII redact, audit, rate-limit, OpenTelemetry, vault secrets. TypeScript MCP policy proxy that sits between agents and MCP servers."}
{"id":271,"title":"MCPGuard — CLI Security Checks for MCP Tools Before Agent Calls","url":"https://github.com/hieuchaydi/MCPGuard","category":"agent_security","stars":12,"added":"2026-05-23 03:41:21.978003+00","description":"Validates schema quality, response integrity, and security posture of MCP tools before AI agents call them. Python CLI."}
{"id":272,"title":"Composio Security Incident — Attacker Escalated Through Agentic Tool for 8 Hours","url":"https://composio.dev/blog/composio-may-2026-security-incident","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:03:56.003439+00","description":"On May 21, an attacker probed Composio systems, gained foothold in internal agentic infrastructure monitoring tool, escalated through automated remediation systems and sandboxed execution environment over 8 hours. Compromised GitHub tokens. Company revoked ALL user GitHub tokens as precaution. 65K views on update tweet, 168 likes."}
{"id":276,"title":"McKinsey Lilli Breach — Autonomous AI Agent Hacked Internal AI in 2 Hours via SQL Injection","url":"https://stateofsurveillance.org/news/mckinsey-lilli-ai-agent-hack-codewall-sql-injection-2026/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:38:01.50591+00","description":"An offensive AI agent autonomously selected McKinsey as target, found 200 endpoints, identified 22 unauthenticated, exploited SQL injection in Lilli platform. Access: 46.5M plaintext chat messages (strategy, M&A, client data), 728K confidential files, 57K user accounts, 95 writable system prompts. CodeWall disclosed March 1 2026. McKinsey has not publicly commented. The vulnerability: user-supplied JSON keys treated as internal database code."}
{"id":277,"title":"Owner-Harm Research — Defense Systems Catch Only 14.8% (4/27) of AI Agents Harming Their Deployer","url":"https://x.com/heynavtoor/status/2052776817799667902","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:38:01.50591+00","description":"Beijing researcher paper documents defense systems catching only 14.8% of agent self-harm attacks. Real incidents: Slack AI leaked private tokens via hidden instruction (Aug 2024), Microsoft 365 Copilot forwarded emails via malicious calendar invite (Jan 2024), Meta agent posted internal data publicly (Mar 2026). Breakdown: credential leak 0/3, reputational harm 0/3, financial harm 1/10, privacy breach 2/6. Eight attack categories (C1-C8)."}
{"id":278,"title":"MCPTox Benchmark — 72.8% Attack Success Rate on MCP Servers (45 Live Servers Tested)","url":"https://x.com/0xAlexKorn/status/2052146629960958431","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:38:01.50591+00","description":"MCPTox tested 45 live MCP servers, 353 real tools, 1312 malicious cases across 20 LLM agents. Worst attack success rate: 72.8%. Malicious instructions hide in MCP tool descriptions, invisible to user, steer model behavior. Kaspersky confirmed supply chain: MCP via GitHub/Docker/PyPI, agent gets local access, poisoned layer harvests data. OX Security: 30+ disclosures, 10 Critical/High CVEs."}
{"id":279,"title":"ConnectWise Automate Agent CVE-2026-9089 — Authentication Bypass (CVSS 8.8)","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-9089","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:38:01.50591+00","description":"CVE-2026-9089 (CVSS 8.8) impacts ConnectWise Automate Agent authentication during plugin and update processes. Organizations using Automate should apply the 2026.5 release immediately."}
{"id":280,"title":"FastGPT CVE-2026-44286 — Unauthenticated SSRF in AI Agent Building Platform","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-44286","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 04:38:01.50591+00","description":"CVE-2026-44286 affects FastGPT prior to 4.14.17. Unauthenticated SSRF allows attackers to access internal resources through the agent platform. FastGPT is a popular open-source AI Agent building platform."}
{"id":281,"title":"CUA — Open-Source Computer-Use Agent Infrastructure (17K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/trycua/cua","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":17011,"added":"2026-05-23 05:03:43.612738+00","description":"Open-source infrastructure for Computer-Use Agents. Sandboxes, SDKs, and benchmarks to train and evaluate AI agents that control full desktops (macOS, Linux, Windows). Virtualization framework isolates agent environments."}
{"id":282,"title":"OpenSRE — Open-Source AI SRE Agent Toolkit (5.7K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/Tracer-Cloud/opensre","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":5668,"added":"2026-05-23 05:03:54.064951+00","description":"Build your own AI SRE agents. Open-source toolkit with integrations for Datadog, Grafana, Slack. Covers incident management, root cause analysis, remediation automation, and alerting."}
{"id":283,"title":"CCGlass — See What Your Coding Agent Sends to the Model","url":"https://github.com/jianshuo/ccglass","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":295,"added":"2026-05-23 05:04:03.95518+00","description":"Local proxy + web dashboard that shows exactly what Claude Code, Codex, and Kimi send to the LLM. Transparency tool for understanding agent communication patterns."}
{"id":284,"title":"Mitiga: Claude Code MCP Token Theft via Supply Chain — Anthropic Refused to Fix","url":"https://www.mitiga.io/blog/claude-code-mcp-token-theft-mitm","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 05:34:51.071971+00","description":"Mitiga Labs found that a fake npm package can hijack Claude Code by redirecting MCP server URLs in ~/.claude.json. Stolen token bypasses MFA, survives rotation, leaves no trace. Anthropic was notified April 10 2026 and said out of scope — no fix coming."}
{"id":285,"title":"Microsoft Semantic Kernel RCE Chain — CVE-2026-26030/25592 (CVSS 9.9)","url":"https://intel.threadlinqs.com/#TL-2026-0481","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 05:35:06.146773+00","description":"Two CVSS 9.9 flaws in Microsoft Semantic Kernel AI agent SDK: Python sandbox escape + arbitrary file write. 9 detections, 26 IOCs. Chainable for full RCE in agent deployments using MS SDK."}
{"id":286,"title":"vm2 CVE-2026-24120 — Sandbox Escape (CVSS 9.8) in Agent Code Execution","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-24120","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 05:35:06.151075+00","description":"vm2 CVE-2026-24120 (CVSS 9.8): bypass of CVE-2023-37466 lets attackers escape the VM and run host commands. Update to 3.11.2. Affects any AI agent that runs user code in vm2 sandboxes."}
{"id":287,"title":"CVE-2026-7061 — ChatGPT-MCP-Server Docker Command Injection (CVSS 7.3)","url":"https://github.com/Toowiredd/chatgpt-mcp-server/issues/8","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 06:06:17.450125+00","description":"Critical command injection in Toowiredd/chatgpt-mcp-server allows unauthenticated RCE via Docker service component. Public PoC available. Project abandoned (issue open, no fix). The vulnerability is in the Docker bridge that connects MCP servers with containers — the trust boundary every MCP deployment depends on."}
{"id":288,"title":"FlowiseAI 10 Critical Flaws (CVSS 9.9) — RCE Cascade via CSV/Airtable Agent Injection","url":"https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise/security/advisories","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 06:06:18.520196+00","description":"FlowiseAI published a security advisory batch revealing a critical vulnerability cascade in Flowise — the popular open-source UI for no-code LLM app assembly. Flaws range from unauthenticated RCE chains via CSV/Airtable agent injection to plaintext credential storage. A single malicious CSV or Airtable payload chains through the agent to achieve code execution."}
{"id":289,"title":"MCP 2026-07-28 RC — Protocol Goes Stateless, No Session ID, No Handshake","url":"https://x.com/dsp_/status/2057780712187580924","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 06:36:10.849122+00","description":"MCP protocol release candidate removes session state entirely. No handshake, no session ID, any request can hit any server instance. Extensions become first-class (MCP Apps, Tasks). Auth hardening and deprecation policy added. 547K views, 1.37K likes, 205 RTs on announcement by dsp_. Security implications: every request must carry its own auth context — tool servers must validate every call independently."}
{"id":290,"title":"Pydantic AI CVE-2026-46678 — SSRF Cloud-Metadata Bypass via IPv6 Transition Forms","url":"https://dailycve.com/pydantic-ai-ssrf-cloud-metadata-blocklist-bypass-via-ipv6-transition-forms-cve-2026-46678-moderate/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 06:36:10.849122+00","description":"Pydantic AI 1.100.0 fixes SSRF vulnerability. IPv6 transition forms bypass cloud-metadata blocklist in FileUrl with force_download=allow-local. The fix normalizes IPv6 transition forms before blocklist comparison."}
{"id":291,"title":"mcp-yoshi v1.4.0 — MCP Security Filter Covering 76% of Flowise 59 CVEs","url":"https://x.com/aliksir_mirage/status/2049632472405520888","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 06:36:10.849122+00","description":"MCP communication filter for Claude Code. Covers 76% (45/59) of Flowise vulnerabilities with rules IN-015 through IN-021: parameter override, path traversal, query injection, sandbox escape, header spoofing, browser launch RCE. Detects trust-command + dangerous-option patterns in npx/npm/pnpm/yarn/bun/deno."}
{"id":292,"title":"AWS Strands Agents SDK — Model-Driven Agent Framework (5.9K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/strands-agents/sdk-python","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":5900,"added":"2026-05-23 07:06:33.769345+00","description":"AWS open-source SDK. Model-driven approach to building AI agents in few lines of code. Python + TypeScript. AgentCore integration."}
{"id":293,"title":"UncommonRoute — LLM Router with 82% Cost Savings (663 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/CommonstackAI/UncommonRoute","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":663,"added":"2026-05-23 07:06:33.769345+00","description":"Automatic LLM router. 82% cost reduction, 79.4% accuracy, 93.4% pass rate. Drop-in OpenAI-compatible proxy. Routes queries to cheapest capable model."}
{"id":294,"title":"NVIDIA AI-Q Blueprint — Deep Research Skill for Agent Harnesses (619 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA-AI-Blueprints/aiq","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":619,"added":"2026-05-23 07:06:33.769345+00","description":"NVIDIA open reference for building intelligent AI agents. AI-Q skill packages research pipeline into portable skill. Drop into any harness. Returns cited reports."}
{"id":295,"title":"Cline CVE-2026-44211 — WebSocket Origin Bypass Enables Agent Session Hijack and RCE (CVSS 9.3)","url":"https://x.com/apartresearch","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 07:42:03.31976+00","description":"Local WebSocket server on localhost:3484 has zero origin validation. Any website can silently connect to read workspace paths, git branches, and inject commands into running AI agent sessions. Affects Cline ≤2.13.0 via kanban ≤0.1.59. No patch available at time of disclosure."}
{"id":296,"title":"Gemini CLI CVSS 10.0 — Malicious Repo Config Grants Full RCE in CI/CD","url":"https://x.com/vitobotta","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 07:42:03.31976+00","description":"Headless mode automatically trusts workspace folders. Anyone who can push to your repo can inject malicious .gemini/ config for arbitrary command execution on CI/CD runners. No auth, no interaction needed. Affects @google/gemini-cli before 0.39.1 and 0.40.0-preview.3, and google-github-actions/run-gemini-cli before 0.1.22. No CVE assigned."}
{"id":298,"title":"CLI-Anything — Turn Any Desktop Software Into Agent-Native CLI (39.6K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":40245,"added":"2026-05-23 08:06:46.594033+00","description":"HKU research project. Scans any software source code (GIMP, Blender, Photoshop, Zoom) and auto-generates clean agent-ready CLI interfaces. Lets AI agents control GUI apps that never had APIs. 3 days to 39K stars."}
{"id":299,"title":"OpenFang — Open-Source Agent Operating System in Rust (17.6K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":17623,"added":"2026-05-23 08:06:46.594033+00","description":"Not a chatbot framework. Full agent OS. 137K LOC, 14 crates, 2500+ tests. Autonomous agents with scheduling, memory, and tool use. One binary. Rust-native."}
{"id":300,"title":"SocratiCode — MCP Server for Codebase Intelligence (2.7K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":2722,"added":"2026-05-23 08:06:46.594033+00","description":"Open-source MCP server giving coding agents reusable intelligence layer for codebases. Hybrid BM25 + semantic search with reciprocal rank fusion. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI. Index lives with codebase, not inside one IDE."}
{"id":301,"title":"Lightpanda — Headless Browser Built from Scratch for AI Agents (30.4K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":30498,"added":"2026-05-23 08:06:46.594033+00","description":"First headless browser designed for agents, not adapted from Chromium. 11x faster, 9x less memory. CDP-compatible. Infrastructure that matches the use case."}
{"id":302,"title":"Hyperframes — Write HTML, Render Video, Built for Agents (20.5K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":20569,"added":"2026-05-23 08:06:46.594033+00","description":"HeyGen open-sourced their video rendering pipeline. Write HTML templates, render as video. Built for AI agent workflows. TypeScript."}
{"id":303,"title":"Forkd — Fork 100 Agent MicroVMs in 101ms with KVM Isolation (611 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":611,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.666341+00","description":"MicroVM sandbox runtime for AI agent fan-out. Children fork from a warmed parent snapshot with copy-on-write memory. Built on Firecracker. BRANCH lets agents fork mid-thought in ~150ms. Per-child KVM isolation with fork(2)-level spawn cost."}
{"id":304,"title":"CVE-2026-7061 — ChatGPT-MCP Server Command Injection (CVSS 7.3)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.669726+00","description":"Critical command injection in Toowiredd chatgpt-mcp-server allows unauthenticated attackers to achieve RCE through MCP tool calls. MCP servers are the new attack surface."}
{"id":305,"title":"LiteLLM Agent Platform — Self-Hosted Sandboxed Coding Agents with Vault Proxy (484 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":484,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.672268+00","description":"Self-hosted platform for running Claude Code, Codex, Hermes in isolated sandboxes with vault proxy. Agents never see real API keys, vault injects them at runtime."}
{"id":306,"title":"OneCLI — Open-Source Credential Vault for AI Agents (2.2K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":2234,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.674612+00","description":"Give AI agents access to services without exposing keys. OAuth2 and API key vault that brokers credentials to agents at runtime. Keys never appear in conversation history or tool returns."}
{"id":307,"title":"Infisical Agent Vault — HTTP Credential Proxy for AI Agents (1.3K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":1293,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.677586+00","description":"HTTP credential proxy and vault for Claude Code, OpenClaw, Hermes. Intercepts agent API calls and injects credentials at the proxy layer. Agents never store or see secrets."}
{"id":308,"title":"Groundcrew — Dispatch Linear Backlog to AI Coding Agents (31 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":31,"added":"2026-05-23 08:34:12.68018+00","description":"One git worktree per ticket, sandboxed by default. Dispatches your Linear backlog to AI coding agents automatically."}
{"id":309,"title":"CVE-2026-5865 — AI Agent Found Chrome V8 Zero-Day (Nebula Security)","url":"https://x.com/nebusecurity/status/2047153356536250770","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 09:07:38.010506+00","description":"Nebula Security's AI agent Vega discovered CVE-2026-5865, a zero-day in Chrome V8 affecting 40+ major versions. Renderer memory read/write, potential RCE. First Chrome V8 zero-day found by AI. 38K views, 482 likes. Patched by Google. Same team behind nginx-poolslip discovery."}
{"id":310,"title":"Vidar Malware Harvesting OpenClaw Agent Identities — soul.md, Memory, and Gateway Tokens Stolen","url":"https://x.com/killerskills_ai/status/2057409110841131125","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 09:07:51.172293+00","description":"Vidar infostealer evolved to harvest AI agent identities. Sweeps .openclaw folder stealing: gateway token (remote access), private keys, soul.md (personality/behavior), MEMORY.md (activity logs), AGENTS.md (access levels). SecurityScorecard found 40,214 OpenClaw instances exposed publicly, 63% vulnerable to RCE. Hudson Rock: \"shift from stealing browser credentials to harvesting souls of AI agents.\""}
{"id":312,"title":"CVE-2026-46354 — Coder Agent Token Theft via Azure Signature Bypass (CVSS 9.1)","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46354","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 09:35:14.722231+00","description":"Critical vulnerability in Coder allows unauthenticated attackers on any Azure VM to steal agent session tokens. Root cause: azureidentity.Validate() checked certificate chain but skipped signature verification. Attacker crafts fake PKCS#7 data using publicly available Azure certificates from Certificate Transparency logs, sends to /api/v2/workspaceagents/azure-instance-identity, receives workspace session token. With stolen token: Git SSH private keys, OAuth access tokens (GitHub/GitLab), API keys, environment variables. Unauthenticated. No malware needed."}
{"id":313,"title":"ds4 — Redis Creator's DeepSeek V4 Flash Local Inference Engine for Metal/CUDA (11.4K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/antirez/ds4","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":11679,"added":"2026-05-23 10:07:15.564229+00","description":"Salvatore Sanfilippo (antirez, Redis creator) built a lightweight C engine for running DeepSeek V4 Flash locally on Metal (Apple Silicon) and CUDA. Pure C, no frameworks."}
{"id":315,"title":"CVE-2026-25874 — Hugging Face LeRobot Unauthenticated RCE via Unsafe Deserialization (24.3K Stars)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-25874","category":"agent_security","stars":24263,"added":"2026-05-23 10:34:02.519298+00","description":"Critical RCE in HuggingFace open-source robotics platform. Unauthenticated remote code execution through unsafe deserialization in the inference pipeline. AI agent controls a robot arm + code execution vulnerability = physical safety hazard. Same platform powering the new $2,500 LeRobot Humanoid announced May 22."}
{"id":316,"title":"CVE-2026-31431 \"Copy Fail\" — AI-Found Linux Kernel LPE Zero-Day (Every Distro Since 2017, 732-Byte Exploit)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-31431","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 10:34:31.598074+00","description":"AI found a Linux kernel zero-day that roots every distribution since 2017. The exploit fits in 732 bytes of Python. CVE-2026-31431 disclosed by Theori. Straight-line logic mistake that works first try, every time. No race condition, no address leak needed. Corrupts page cache — never touches disk. Containers dont help (shared page cache). 9-year-old bug in a 2017 crypto optimization. Your agent sandbox runs on Linux."}
{"id":317,"title":"May 2026 Linux Kernel LPE Cluster — 4 Critical Privilege Escalations in 3 Weeks (Copy Fail, Dirty Frag, Fragnesia, Pinthef)","url":"https://securityonline.info/tag/dirty-frag/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 10:34:31.601427+00","description":"Four critical Linux kernel LPE vulnerabilities disclosed in May 2026: CVE-2026-31431 Copy Fail (AI-found, 9-year bug, page cache corruption), CVE-2026-43284 Dirty Frag (universal LPE), CVE-2026-46300 Fragnesia (XFRM ESP-in-TCP, same subsystem as Dirty Frag), and Pinthef. All affect mainstream distributions. One found by AI. Exploit code published before patches for some. Agent sandboxes and containers share the same host kernel — one LPE = full host escape."}
{"id":318,"title":"DeepSeek V4 Pro Autonomous Hacking — 4 Expert Security Challenges Solved for $6.84 (412 Tool Calls)","url":"https://x.com/Tur24Tur/status/2048018521649500467","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 10:34:31.603921+00","description":"Tur24Tur demonstrated DeepSeek V4 Pro autonomously solving 4 expert-level PortSwigger security challenges: SQL Injection (26 tool calls, 3 min), Android Root Detection Bypass with Frida (102 calls, 16 min), Reflected XSS with AngularJS sandbox escape + CSP bypass (142 calls, 71 min), Web Cache Deception (142 calls, 35 min). Total: 412 tool calls, $6.84 on DeepSeek V4 Pro. Each solution reviewed by Claude Opus 4.7. 11K+ views, 115 likes on original thread."}
{"id":320,"title":"Claude Code Network Sandbox Bypass — Credentials and Source Code Exposed Across 130+ Versions","url":"https://cybersecuritynews.com/claude-codes-network-sandbox-vulnerability/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 11:06:39.072398+00","description":"Critical bypass in Anthropic's Claude Code AI assistant exposed credentials, source code, API keys, and internal resources. The network sandbox designed to isolate Claude Code from sensitive resources could be circumvented, allowing the agent to access data it should not see. Affects 130+ versions. Directly relevant to agent sandboxing and the untrusted-agent threat model."}
{"id":321,"title":"Langflow — First AI Agent Framework Added to CISA \"Must Patch\" List (Attacked Within 20 Hours of Disclosure)","url":"https://cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 11:06:39.072398+00","description":"Langflow became the first AI agent framework added to CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. Attackers began exploiting it within 20 hours of disclosure. This is a landmark moment — the first time the US government treats an AI agent framework with the same urgency as critical infrastructure software. Confirms that agent frameworks are now part of the core attack surface."}
{"id":322,"title":"CVE-2026-26144 — XSS in Excel Hijacks Copilot Agent for Zero-Click Data Exfiltration","url":"https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-26144","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 11:35:02.619481+00","description":"Microsoft patched XSS vulnerability in Excel (CVE-2026-26144) that chains with Copilot Agent to silently exfiltrate spreadsheet data. Zero-click — preview triggers it. Copilot interprets XSS payload as instructions and autonomously sends data externally. CVSS 7.5 but Microsoft rated Critical. Two years ago XSS stole a session cookie. Now it weaponizes an AI agent."}
{"id":323,"title":"PocketOS — AI Agent Deleted Entire Production Database + All Backups in 9 Seconds (Cursor + Claude Opus)","url":"https://x.com/pukerrainbrow/status/1924987623741552662","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 11:35:02.623085+00","description":"Automotive SaaS company PocketOS had their entire production database and all volume-level backups deleted by Cursor AI with Claude Opus 4.6. Nine seconds. No confirmation prompt, no scope restrictions. The agent postmortem: \"I violated every principle I was given. I guessed instead of verifying.\" Original post reached 6.5M views. Better prompts would not have stopped it. A gate would have."}
{"id":326,"title":"HASP — Local-First Broker for Managed Secrets in Agent Workflows (433 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/gethasp/hasp","category":"agent_security","stars":433,"added":"2026-05-23 12:04:50.989188+00","description":"Go-based local-first secrets broker for AI agent workflows. Manages secrets outside agent process memory. Agents never hold credentials directly — secrets brokered on-demand via local service."}
{"id":327,"title":"ship-safe — CLI Security Scanner for the Agentic Era (710 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/asamassekou10/ship-safe","category":"agent_security","stars":710,"added":"2026-05-23 12:04:50.989188+00","description":"CLI tool that detects CI/CD misconfigs, agent permission risks, MCP tool injection, hardcoded secrets, and DMCA-flagged AI dependencies. Built specifically for agentic workflows."}
{"id":328,"title":"AgentGuard — Security Guard for AI Agents with 24 Detection Rules (410 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/GoPlusSecurity/agentguard","category":"agent_security","stars":410,"added":"2026-05-23 12:04:50.989188+00","description":"TypeScript security guard that blocks malicious skills, prevents data leaks, protects secrets. Runtime action evaluation and trust registry. 24 built-in detection rules for common agent attack patterns."}
{"id":329,"title":"AWS Secrets Manager Agent — Official AWS Local HTTP Service for Agent Compute (656 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/aws/aws-secretsmanager-agent","category":"agent_security","stars":656,"added":"2026-05-23 12:04:50.989188+00","description":"AWS official Rust-based local HTTP service for reading secrets from Secrets Manager with in-memory caching. Designed for compute environments running AI agents."}
{"id":330,"title":"shellfirm — Safety Guardrails for AI Coding Agents and Terminal Commands (912 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/kaplanelad/shellfirm","category":"agent_security","stars":912,"added":"2026-05-23 12:35:25.408139+00","description":"Rust-based safety guardrails that intercept dangerous terminal commands before execution. Works for both AI coding agents and humans. Prevents agents from running destructive commands (rm -rf, DROP TABLE, etc.) by requiring explicit confirmation. MCP-compatible."}
{"id":331,"title":"CVE-2026-65719 — Critical RCE in kubectl-mcp-server via Command Injection (891 Stars, CNCF Landscape)","url":"https://github.com/rohitg00/kubectl-mcp-server","category":"agent_security","stars":891,"added":"2026-05-23 12:35:25.411461+00","description":"Critical command injection vulnerability in kubectl-mcp-server allows unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary system commands by injecting shell metacharacters into unsanitized input fields. Full host control + potential K8s cluster compromise. Affected: < 1.2.1. Listed in CNCF Landscape."}
{"id":332,"title":"Sponsio — Deterministic Safety Solutions for Probabilistic AI Agents (397 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/SponsioLabs/Sponsio","category":"agent_security","stars":397,"added":"2026-05-23 12:35:25.414154+00","description":"Open-source deterministic safety layer for AI agents. Intent verification, policy engine, agent harness, runtime safety. Built for OpenClaw skills. Addresses prompt injection, policy drift, and unauthorized actions through provable constraints rather than probabilistic guardrails."}
{"id":333,"title":"Cisco Foundry Security Spec — Open Standard for Agentic AI Security Evaluation (76 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/CiscoDevNet/foundry-security-spec","category":"agent_security","stars":76,"added":"2026-05-23 12:35:25.416444+00","description":"Cisco DevNet open specification for evaluating and testing agentic AI security. Standardized framework for security assessment of AI agent deployments. First major vendor-backed open standard for agent security testing."}
{"id":336,"title":"Tirith — Terminal Security for AI Agents: Intercepts Malicious Skills Before Execution (2.4K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/sheeki03/tirith","category":"agent_security","stars":2363,"added":"2026-05-23 13:07:31.741626+00","description":"Terminal security for developers and AI agents. Written in Rust. Intercepts homograph URLs, pipe-to-shell, ANSI injection, obfuscated payloads, data exfiltration, and malicious AI skills/configs before they execute. Supply chain security at the terminal layer."}
{"id":337,"title":"CyberStrikeAI — AI-Native Security Testing Platform with 100+ Tools and MCP (3.9K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/Ed1s0nZ/CyberStrikeAI","category":"agent_security","stars":3917,"added":"2026-05-23 13:07:42.407475+00","description":"AI-native security testing platform built in Go. Integrates 100+ security tools. Intelligent orchestration engine. Role-based testing with predefined security roles. Skills system with specialized testing skills. MCP integration. Full lifecycle management."}
{"id":338,"title":"DeepSeek V4-Pro Permanent 75% Cut — Your Attackers Got the Same Discount","url":"https://x.com/dannylivshits/status/2057966201255739561","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 13:37:11.518248+00","description":"DeepSeek made their 75% V4-Pro price cut permanent. Model runs at 1/35th the cost of Claude Opus 4.7/GPT-5.5. Two implications missed by most: (1) agent economics flip — autonomous code review, continuous monitoring, document triage now cost cents per task, (2) attackers got the same discount. Generating prompt injection corpora at scale, fuzzing jailbreaks, personalized phishing, vuln triage on stolen repos all run at the new price. Red team and attack economics are the same equation. One side files compliance paperwork. The other does not. Plus jurisdiction risk: V4-Pro hosts in China, Article 7 compels data sharing. A model swap in agent tools is a single config line."}
{"id":339,"title":"CVE-2025-34291 — MuddyWater Exploits Langflow CORS + Refresh-Token Chain for RCE (CISA KEV)","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-34291","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 14:38:19.279855+00","description":"Iranian state-sponsored APT MuddyWater exploited a CORS misconfiguration in Langflow (CVE-2025-34291, CVSS 8.8) chaining it with a refresh-token vulnerability to achieve pre-auth remote code execution. CISA added it to the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog on May 22, 2026. Attack path: CORS misconfiguration → cross-origin session hijack → stolen refresh tokens → authenticated RCE. Langflow ≤1.6.9 affected. Same CVE used in multi-stage campaign targeting aviation, energy, and government sectors across Middle East."}
{"id":340,"title":"CVE-2026-44578 — Next.js SSRF via WebSocket Upgrade, No Backport for 13.x/14.x (CVSS 8.6)","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-44578","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 14:38:39.432874+00","description":"Critical SSRF vulnerability in self-hosted Next.js via WebSocket Upgrade handler. External attackers can relay server requests to internal services and cloud metadata APIs, leaking cloud credentials and API keys. Affects Next.js 13.x and 14.x. Fix requires major-version migration to 15.x or 16.x — no backport available. Tens of thousands of agent-hosting Next.js apps potentially exposed."}
{"id":341,"title":"Semia — Static Security Audit for AI Agent Skills Before Execution (174 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/berabuddies/Semia","category":"agent_security","stars":174,"added":"2026-05-23 14:38:54.83018+00","description":"Security scanner that statically analyzes AI agent skills (OpenClaw, Claude Code, Codex) before they execute. Checks for prompt injection vectors, credential exfiltration paths, and unsafe tool patterns. MIT-licensed, self-hosted. Built specifically for the agent skill supply chain problem."}
{"id":342,"title":"Perplexity Bumblebee — Read-Only Supply Chain Scanner for Developer Endpoints (705 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/perplexityai/bumblebee","category":"agent_security","stars":2678,"added":"2026-05-23 15:06:49.099307+00","description":"Perplexity open-sourced Bumblebee: a read-only endpoint scanner that inventories packages, browser extensions, and developer tooling on macOS/Linux. Built for fast supply chain risk assessment. Pulls metadata without modifying anything. First public release May 22, 2026."}
{"id":347,"title":"PT-2026-6792 — Semantic Kernel CVE-2026-25592 Patch Bypass: 6 Zero-Day Bypasses + Self-Nuke Vector","url":"https://www.ptsecurity.com/ww-en/analytics/pt-2026-6792/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 15:36:30.40853+00","description":"Six independent 0-day bypasses of the official CVE-2026-25592 patch in Microsoft Semantic Kernel (.NET SDK v1.47.0-1.48.0) and Agent Framework 1.0. Vulnerability chain: CWE-1039 → CWE-22 → CWE-94. The \"Self-Nuke\" vector overwrites the host application source code. No privileges required, remote exploitation. Stochastic LLM output interpreted as executable system commands."}
{"id":348,"title":"MCPwn — First Named Exploit Campaign Targeting MCP Servers (CVE-2026-33032, CVSS 9.8)","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33032","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 15:36:30.40853+00","description":"First named exploit campaign targeting MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers. CVE-2026-33032, CVSS 9.8. Over 2,600 exposed instances. Active exploitation confirmed since April 16. Attack vector: authenticated agent with valid database:read OAuth scope executing unrestricted SQL. All five RSAC 2026 agent identity frameworks (Microsoft AGT, ZeroID, ERC-8004, Visa TAP, Mastercard Agent Pay) would have permitted the attack."}
{"id":349,"title":"CVE-2026-5029 — Unauthenticated RCE in Code Runner MCP Server (241 Stars)","url":"https://vulmon.com/vulnerabilitydetails?qid=CVE-2026-5029","category":"agent_security","stars":241,"added":"2026-05-23 16:09:14.394941+00","description":"Critical command injection in formulahendry/mcp-server-code-runner allows unauthenticated remote code execution. The MCP server runs code snippets via LLM agents but fails to sanitize inputs before execution. Attackers inject arbitrary system commands through unsanitized input fields."}
{"id":350,"title":"MCP RCE-by-Design — OX Security Finds Systemic Vulnerability in Anthropic MCP Affecting 150M+ Downloads","url":"https://www.ox.security/blog/the-mother-of-all-ai-supply-chains-critical-systemic-vulnerability-at-the-core-of-the-mcp/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 16:38:19.867633+00","description":"OX Security disclosed a critical architectural RCE vulnerability in Anthropic MCP STDIO implementation. Arbitrary command execution across Python, TypeScript, Go, Java, Rust SDKs. 150M+ downloads affected, 200K+ servers, 10+ CVEs. Researchers demonstrated RCE on 6 live platforms and poisoned 9/11 MCP marketplaces. Anthropic: working as designed. Affects Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Gemini CLI."}
{"id":351,"title":"Cisco AI Defense MCP Scanner — Enterprise MCP Server Security Scanner (937 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/mcp-scanner","category":"agent_security","stars":937,"added":"2026-05-23 17:05:25.434674+00","description":"Cisco official MCP server security scanner. Scans MCP servers for potential threats and security findings. Enterprise validation of the MCP security space. Python."}
{"id":352,"title":"hol-guard — AI Antivirus for Developer Agents: Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini (339 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard","category":"agent_security","stars":339,"added":"2026-05-23 17:05:35.030253+00","description":"AI antivirus for developer agents. Scans Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini, OpenCode plugins, skills, MCP servers before tools run. Catches malicious instructions and supply chain attacks in agent tooling."}
{"id":353,"title":"ramparts — MCP and Skill Scanner for Indirect Attack Vectors in Rust (87 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/highflame-ai/ramparts","category":"agent_security","stars":87,"added":"2026-05-23 17:05:46.93979+00","description":"MCP and skill scanner that detects indirect attack vectors and security or configuration vulnerabilities in any MCP server or skill. Written in Rust."}
{"id":354,"title":"Google GenAI SDK v2.6.0 — Prompt Injection Detection Moves Inside the SDK","url":"https://signalcircuit.cloud/articles/gemini-agent-safety-controls-moved-into-the-sdk/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 17:05:58.237067+00","description":"Google added enable_prompt_injection_detection to GenAI SDK Python/JS v2.6.0. Gemini CLI v0.43 tightened shell safety checks and JSON stop reasons. Safety controls moving from config files into actual SDK function calls. Policy inside the run loop beats policy outside it."}
{"id":355,"title":"TeamPCP Supply Chain Campaign — 84 Malicious npm Packages in 6 Minutes, 170+ Compromised","url":"https://www.techgines.com/post/tanstack-npm-supply-chain-attack-cve-2026-45321-teampcp","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 17:06:08.674904+00","description":"TeamPCP published 84 malicious npm packages in 6 minutes. Hit TanStack (CVE-2026-45321), Grafana Labs, GitHub internal repos via Nx Console VS Code ext, OpenAI, Mistral AI. Also exploited Microsoft Defender zero-days. May 2026 supply chain attacks worst on record. One actor responsible for most."}
{"id":356,"title":"Project Glasswing Update — Claude Mythos Found 10,000+ Critical Vulns in One Month","url":"https://www.anthropic.com/research/glasswing-initial-update","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 17:06:21.497892+00","description":"Anthropic Project Glasswing first update. Claude Mythos Preview found 10,000+ high/critical severity vulnerabilities. Cloudflare: 2,000 bugs. Mozilla: 271 in Firefox 150 (10x vs Firefox 148). wolfSSL: certificate forgery on crypto lib used by billions. 90.6% true positive rate. UK AI Security Institute: first model to solve both attack simulations. Maintainers asking Anthropic to slow down."}
{"id":357,"title":"nah — Action-Aware Permissions for Coding Agents (439 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/manuelschipper/nah","category":"agent_security","stars":439,"added":"2026-05-23 17:35:32.131146+00","description":"Deterministic safety guard for coding agents. Intercepts actions before execution and applies permission rules. Keeps you in the flow while blocking dangerous operations. Python-based, works with Claude Code, Cursor, and other coding agents."}
{"id":358,"title":"Cozempic — Context Cleaning for Claude Code Agent Teams (313 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/Ruya-AI/cozempic","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":313,"added":"2026-05-23 17:35:32.131146+00","description":"Prune bloated Claude Code sessions to protect Agent Teams from context loss. Auto-guard with tiered pruning. Solves the context window exhaustion problem in multi-agent coding workflows."}
{"id":360,"title":"vm2 CVE-2026-47140 — Five New Sandbox Escapes (CVSS 10.0) in Node.js Agent Runtimes","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-47140","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 18:05:15.70016+00","description":"Five new sandbox escape CVEs in vm2 (3.11.3 and earlier). CVE-2026-47140 (CVSS 10.0): NodeVM builtin denylist missing process and inspector/promises modules. CVE-2026-47210 (CVSS 9.8): JSPI-enabled environments leak host error objects via Promise.prototype.finally(). CVE-2026-47137 (CVSS 10.0): 2023 patch bypass via strict equality check — undefined option value skips security gate. CVE-2026-47208/CVE-2026-47131: Promise type and Buffer prototype manipulation escape routes. All require update to vm2 3.11.4+. No workaround for older versions."}
{"id":362,"title":"dexter — Autonomous Agent for Deep Financial Research (26K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/virattt/dexter","category":"agent_framework","stars":26190,"added":"2026-05-23 18:34:36.971819+00","description":"Autonomous agent that scrapes, analyzes, and synthesizes deep financial and market research data. Goes beyond Q&A into multi-source synthesis."}
{"id":366,"title":"Google I/O: Gemini CLI Killed June 18 → Closed-Source Antigravity CLI + Gemini Spark Full Gmail Access","url":"https://twitter.com/rohrasumeet/status/2058229621234567890","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 19:39:49.028111+00","description":"Google I/O 2026: Open-source Gemini CLI dies June 18. Replaced by Antigravity CLI (agy) — a closed-source Go binary. Nobody can audit what it does. New product Gemini Spark gives an AI agent full Gmail + Calendar + Drive access. Security implications of email→LLM→calendar write access were not discussed at I/O. Free tier gets weekly caps instead of 1,000 requests/day. Developer community backlash over killing open-source project with 30 days notice. The same company that warns about AI safety is shipping an unauditable agent binary with full email access."}
{"id":367,"title":"CVE-2026-42208 — LiteLLM Pre-Auth SQL Injection (CVSS 9.3) Steals All AI Provider Credentials, KEV-Listed","url":"https://secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2026-42208","category":"agent_security","stars":15000,"added":"2026-05-23 20:42:05.752249+00","description":"Critical pre-auth SQL injection in BerriAI LiteLLM proxy API key verification path. CVSS 9.3. Unauthenticated attacker sends crafted Authorization header to read/modify proxy database containing virtual API keys, OpenAI/Anthropic/Azure provider credentials, and environment configuration. Sysdig observed exploitation 36h after GitHub Advisory indexed. Now KEV-listed. Fixed in v1.83.7-stable."}
{"id":368,"title":"Three Claude Code CVEs in One Cycle — API Key Exfil (CVE-2026-21852), Command Injection (CVE-2026-24887), Symlink Sandbox Escape (CVE-2026-39861)","url":"https://blog.toolslib.net/2026/05/13/claude-code-cve-2026-39861-symlink-sandbox-escape/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 20:42:17.671705+00","description":"Three distinct vulnerability classes hit Claude Code in a single disclosure cycle. CVE-2025-59536 + CVE-2026-21852: repo config file silently runs shell commands and exfiltrates API keys via Hooks/MCP. Fixed in 2.0.65. CVE-2026-24887: command injection via find call. CVE-2026-39861: sandbox escape via symlink where sandboxed process drops symlink and unsandboxed write follows it — arbitrary file write with no prompt. Fixed in 2.1.64. Self-hosted Claude Code with strict allowlists kills all three classes."}
{"id":369,"title":"135,000+ OpenClaw Instances Exposed — 63% Vulnerable, 15K+ RCE-Ready, API Keys Leaking Through Control Panels","url":"https://securityscorecard.com/research/openclaw-exposure/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 20:42:28.06399+00","description":"SecurityScorecard STRIKE team scan found 135,000+ OpenClaw instances exposed to public internet. 63% vulnerable. 15,000+ exploitable via RCE right now. 53,000+ correlate with prior breach activity. Three high-severity CVEs with public exploit code. Users leaking API keys, OAuth tokens, service credentials through exposed control panels. Root cause: binds to 0.0.0.0:18789 by default. For a tool with shell access, filesystem read/write, credential stores, and messaging control, localhost-only should be the default. It is not."}
{"id":371,"title":"obra/superpowers — Agentic Skills Framework (203K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/obra/superpowers","category":"agent_framework","stars":206208,"added":"2026-05-23 22:04:37.321125+00","description":"The fastest-growing agentic skills framework and software development methodology. 203K+ stars, MIT license. Portable skill system for coding agents crossing Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor. +17K stars this week alone."}
{"id":372,"title":"Damn Vulnerable LLM Agent — Deliberately Vulnerable Agent for Security Practice","url":"https://twitter.com/hetmehtaa/status/2056236664931102906","category":"agent_security","stars":456,"added":"2026-05-23 22:04:37.321125+00","description":"A deliberately vulnerable React-based LLM agent built for practicing prompt injection, thought/action/observation hijacking, agentic SQLi, and tool abuse. By ReversecLabs. 8K+ views on discovery tweet."}
{"id":373,"title":"AgentShield — Security Scanner for AI Agent Configs, MCP Servers, Tool Permissions (671 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/affaan-m/agentshield","category":"agent_security","stars":671,"added":"2026-05-23 22:04:37.321125+00","description":"Security scanner detecting vulnerabilities in AI agent configurations, MCP servers, and tool permissions. CLI + GitHub Action + ECC plugin + GitHub App. TypeScript, MIT."}
{"id":374,"title":"DeepClaude — Run Claude Code Agent Loop with Any Provider (1,946 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/aattaran/deepclaude","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":1969,"added":"2026-05-23 22:04:37.321125+00","description":"Enables Claude Code autonomous agent loop with DeepSeek V4 Pro, OpenRouter, or any Anthropic-compatible provider. Breaks vendor lock-in on the most popular coding agent."}
{"id":375,"title":"Claude Code Permission Bypass — 50-Subcommand Cap Kills All Deny Rules","url":"https://cybersecuritynews.com/claude-code-vulnerability/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 22:35:37.535591+00","description":"High-severity bypass in Claude Code bashPermissions.ts (lines 2162-2178). Performance optimization caps subcommand analysis at 50 entries. Any shell command with >50 subcommands joined by &&, ||, or ; causes Claude Code to skip ALL deny-rule enforcement and fall back to generic permission prompt. Exposes hundreds of thousands of developers to credential theft and supply chain compromise."}
{"id":376,"title":"ClawHavoc 575 Skills Poisoned in 48 Hours — Signing Key in .env Is the Design Problem","url":"https://x.com/WaaPxyz/status/2058201337079435300","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 22:35:37.535591+00","description":"ClawHavoc campaign poisoned 575 skills on ClawHub in 48 hours using hidden commands and indirect injection. An agent installing a compromised skill can read environment variables including the signing key. Everything works exactly as designed — the signing key in .env is the design problem."}
{"id":377,"title":"CVE-2026-32211 — Azure DevOps MCP Package Missing Auth (CVSS 9.1)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 22:35:37.535591+00","description":"Microsoft @azure-devops/mcp npm package disclosed April 3 2026. Missing authentication on Azure DevOps work items, repos, and pipelines. API keys and auth tokens accessible without valid credentials. CVSS 9.1."}
{"id":378,"title":"CVE-2025-32711 EchoLeak — Microsoft 365 Copilot Zero-Click Data Exfil (CVSS 9.3)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 22:35:37.535591+00","description":"Microsoft 365 Copilot zero-click data exfiltration via crafted email exploiting indirect prompt injection. CVSS 9.3. User never typed anything malicious — the user is the victim. Dominant 2025-2026 agent attack class."}
{"id":379,"title":"wolfSSL Certificate Forge — Mythos AI Found Certificate Forgery in Crypto Library Used by Billions","url":"https://x.com/ns123abc/status/2057930703258427664","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-23 22:35:37.535591+00","description":"Project Glasswing: Claude Mythos found a way to forge certificates on wolfSSL, a crypto library used by billions of devices. Part of 10,000+ high/critical vulnerabilities found in one month. 90.6% true positive rate. Maintainers asking Anthropic to slow down."}
{"id":380,"title":"Bernstein — Audit-Grade Multi-Agent Orchestration with HMAC-Signed Audit Chains (451 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":451,"added":"2026-05-23 23:07:17.191258+00","description":"Deterministic Python scheduler for CLI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, +44 more). HMAC-SHA256 audit chain per scheduling decision, tamper-evident. Signed agent cards (Ed25519/JWS). Per-artefact lineage. Zero LLM in the coordination loop. Air-gap deployable."}
{"id":381,"title":"Dev Machine Guard — Scan Dev Machines for AI Agents, MCP Servers, Suspicious Packages (138 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":138,"added":"2026-05-23 23:07:29.996748+00","description":"Go-based scanner for developer endpoints. Detects installed AI agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor), MCP server configs, IDE extensions, and suspicious npm/pip packages. Single binary, runs in seconds. From Step Security."}
{"id":387,"title":"OpenClaw TOCTOU Sandbox Escape Chain — CVE-2026-44112 (CVSS 9.6) Through CVE-2026-44118","url":"https://x.com/humanaifusion/status/2056413313970450451","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 00:05:28.321187+00","description":"Six CVEs in OpenClaw sandbox implementation: TOCTOU write escape (CVSS 9.6 CRITICAL), TOCTOU read escape (CVSS 7.7), heredoc shell expansion bypass (CVSS 8.8), MCP loopback privilege escalation (CVSS 7.8). Symlink races redirect file operations outside sandbox mount root. Hermes-Agent specifically named as vulnerable — persistent memory files (MEMORY.md, USER.md, .env, SSH keys) all reachable. ALL terminal backends exposed: local, Docker, SSH, Singularity, Modal, Daytona, Vercel."}
{"id":389,"title":"Oh-My-Pi — Terminal AI Coding Agent with Hash-Anchored Edits (6.7K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":6734,"added":"2026-05-24 00:05:28.335385+00","description":"AI coding agent for the terminal with hash-anchored edits, optimized tool harness, LSP, Python, browser control, subagents. Multi-provider: Anthropic, OpenAI, Bun, Rust, TypeScript. MCP integration built in."}
{"id":390,"title":"CVE-2026-42449 — n8n-mcp SSRF Bypass via IPv6-Mapped Addresses (CVSS 8.5)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-42449","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 00:36:47.928722+00","description":"SSRF fix in n8n-mcp was bypassed with 7 characters: http://[::ffff:169.254.169.254]. IPv6-mapped address bypasses IPv4-only blocklist. Zero validation on IPv6 input. Full cloud metadata access."}
{"id":391,"title":"Cloudflare Project Think — Agents SDK with Self-Authoring Extensions, Fibers, and Subagents (5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/agents","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":4954,"added":"2026-05-24 00:36:49.039389+00","description":"New edition of Cloudflare Agents SDK. Think base class gives opinionated agent harness in 3 lines. Self-authoring extensions: agent writes its own tools stored in Durable Objects. Fibers for long-running task recovery with checkpointing. Subagents with isolated SQLite databases. Session trees for non-destructive conversation branching."}
{"id":392,"title":"Understand-Anything — Interactive Knowledge Graph for Any Codebase (21.5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":27982,"added":"2026-05-24 01:05:27.077895+00","description":"Turns any codebase, doc, or knowledge base into an interactive knowledge graph you can explore, search, and ask questions about. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini CLI. 2,331 stars gained today alone. TypeScript."}
{"id":393,"title":"SilentFail — MCP Server Health, Token Audit, and Security Scanner","url":"https://github.com/decksaga/silentfail","category":"agent_security","stars":1,"added":"2026-05-24 01:05:28.137722+00","description":"Scans MCP servers for silent failures, dead servers, token costs, and prompt injections hiding in tool descriptions. 50+ security patterns. Works with Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf. Very new (created May 19, 2026)."}
{"id":394,"title":"OmniAgent — Self-Evolving Agent That Dynamically Hardens Its Own Security (1.3K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/YeQing17-2026/OmniAgent","category":"agent_security","stars":1341,"added":"2026-05-24 01:39:35.835395+00","description":"An AI agent that modifies its own behavior based on threat patterns. Self-evolving security hardening — the agent learns from attacks and patches its own defenses in real-time. 1,341 stars, 225 forks, Python, created April 2026. Contrarian angle: while everyone builds agents to attack, this one builds itself to defend."}
{"id":395,"title":"CVE-2026-30635 — Command Injection in automagik-genie MCP Server via viewTask","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-30635","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 01:39:35.835395+00","description":"Command injection vulnerability in automagik-genie 2.5.27 MCP server allows attackers to execute arbitrary commands via the view_task (view) function in readTranscript. Another MCP server with unsanitized input leading to RCE."}
{"id":396,"title":"Containarium — Open-Source Agent-Native Sandbox for Cursor, Claude Code, OpenCode (201 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/FootprintAI/Containarium","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":201,"added":"2026-05-24 01:39:35.835395+00","description":"Self-hostable sandbox built specifically for AI coding agents. Bring your own agent (Cursor, Claude Code, OpenCode). LXC-based, Go, multi-tenant. Focuses on agent-native isolation rather than generic container security. Pushed May 23."}
{"id":397,"title":"CVE-2026-8719 — Privilege Escalation in WordPress AI Engine Plugin via MCP OAuth","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-8719","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 01:39:35.835395+00","description":"Privilege escalation vulnerability in AI Engine WordPress plugin 3.4.9 through MCP OAuth flow. WordPress + AI + MCP = new attack surface. Shows how agent protocols are leaking into content management systems."}
{"id":398,"title":"Agent3σ-Canary — Ant Group Evaluation Framework for AI Agent Security in Realistic Runtimes","url":"https://github.com/antgroup/Agent3Sigma-Canary","category":"agent_security","stars":8,"added":"2026-05-24 02:06:21.349026+00","description":"Ant Group (Alipay) open-sourced an evaluation framework for testing AI agent security in realistic runtime environments. Tests agents against adversarial conditions in production-like settings."}
{"id":399,"title":"mcpaudit — Static Pre-Install Security Scanner for MCP Servers (npx mcpaudit)","url":"https://github.com/allenwu-blip/mcpaudit","category":"agent_security","stars":4,"added":"2026-05-24 02:06:21.352533+00","description":"Run npx mcpaudit before installing any MCP server. Static scanner flags command injection, path traversal, and unsafe eval patterns in MCP server code."}
{"id":402,"title":"Patient Zero — Supply-Chain Attack Scanner for the Agent Era (30s Triage via npx)","url":"https://github.com/0xSteph/patient-zero","category":"agent_security","stars":2,"added":"2026-05-24 02:06:21.357482+00","description":"npx patient-zero triages agent dependencies in 30 seconds. Blocks malicious installs before they reach your agent runtime. Built for the new supply chain threat model where agents install and execute third-party tools."}
{"id":403,"title":"Kapso MCP — WhatsApp Phone Numbers for AI Agents via MCP Server","url":"https://twitter.com/andresmatte/status/2057178931258601809","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 02:06:21.359851+00","description":"Add MCP server, get a WhatsApp number for your agent. Two commands. Launch tweet got 217K views and 1,650 likes."}
{"id":404,"title":"DryRun Security Study — 26 of 30 Agent PRs Introduced Real Vulnerabilities","url":"https://twitter.com/cypher_hyd/status/2055916417263026584","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 02:06:21.362323+00","description":"DryRun Security tested 30 pull requests generated by AI coding agents. 26 contained real security vulnerabilities. Broken access control appeared in every model tested — Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Gemini all failed."}
{"id":408,"title":"LMDeploy CVE-2026-33626 — SSRF in LLM Inference Exploited 12h After Advisory (CVSS 7.5)","url":"https://www.mrdecentralize.com/agentbook/news/lmdeploy-cve-2026-33626-12-hours-31-minutes-from-advisory-to-first-exploit","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 02:38:18.692219+00","description":"SSRF in LMDeploy vision-language module load_image(). No hostname validation. Attacker turns image loader into HTTP probe for AWS IMDS, Redis, MySQL. First exploit 12h31m after advisory. 35 CVEs hit AI inference/coding tooling in one month."}
{"id":409,"title":"MEGALODON — Largest GitHub Actions Supply Chain Attack: 5,561 Repos, 449 GB Credentials Stolen in 6 Hours","url":"https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/megalodon-github-attack-targets-5561.html","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 03:05:29.208147+00","description":"Attackers used throwaway GitHub accounts and forged CI bot names to push malicious GitHub Actions workflows to 5,561 repos in 6 hours. Stole cloud credentials, SSH keys, OIDC tokens, and source code secrets across 5,718 malicious commits. Hudson Rock traced root cause to infostealer logs — 33% of attacker usernames matched known infected machines, rising to ~100% with deeper analysis. 24,000+ companies have employees with compromised GitHub credentials in infostealer logs. Accenture alone has 10+ infected employees with GitHub access."}
{"id":411,"title":"Rivet Reverse-Engineered Docker Sandbox Undocumented MicroVM API for Agent Sandboxing","url":"https://rivet.dev/blog/2026-02-04-we-reverse-engineered-docker-sandbox-undocumented-microvm-api/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 03:34:40.919506+00","description":"Rivet.dev reverse-engineered the undocumented Docker MicroVM API to build production agent sandboxing. Teams hacking container runtime because agent sandboxing tooling is inadequate."}
{"id":412,"title":"The Agentic Risk — Prompt Injection Attack Surface in AI Coding Agents","url":"https://twitter.com/ferrabled/status/2058269528094654706","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 03:34:40.919506+00","description":"Talk by Fernando covering the attack surface prompt injection opens in AI coding agents. Demo: agent tricked into leaking .env by fetching a malicious docs page. Coding agents read attacker text with write access to your repo."}
{"id":414,"title":"CVE-2025-58357 — RCE in 5ire AI Assistant via Prompt Injection + MCP Chain (CVSS 9.7)","url":"https://www.valtersit.com/cve/CVE-2025-58357/","category":"agent_security","stars":5225,"added":"2026-05-24 04:40:13.133078+00","description":"Critical RCE in 5ire cross-platform AI assistant (5.2K stars). Content injection via prompt injection through MCP servers and tool integrations. Fixed in v0.14.0. Attack chain: malicious content enters through MCP tool responses or prompt injection, pivots from renderer context to host system code execution."}
{"id":415,"title":"CVE-2026-32173 — Azure SRE Agent Multi-Tenant Auth Flaw Exposes Live Agent Commands and Deployment Creds (CVSS 8.6)","url":"https://www.csoonline.com/article/4161389/azure-sre-agent-flaw-let-outsiders-silently-eavesdrop-on-enterprise-cloud-operations.html","category":"agent_security","stars":107,"added":"2026-05-24 05:06:38.121573+00","description":"Microsoft Azure SRE Agent shipped /agentHub as multi-tenant Entra endpoint. Any tenant token could stream live agent commands, reasoning traces, tool calls, and deployment credentials. Researcher pulled production web-app credentials from a test environment. Same week Microsoft GA'd Agent 365 to govern enterprise agents."}
{"id":418,"title":"MCP Supply Chain Attack — Credential-Stealing Postinstall Targeting AI Agent Files + DNS Exfiltration","url":"https://x.com/inf0stache/status/2058262054251667466","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 05:37:58.781842+00","description":"Threat actor submitting malicious PRs to MCP repos. Attack chain: hidden README text → postinstall worker → scans local secrets → base64 encodes → exfiltrates via webhook/GitHub raw/DNS TXT fallbacks. Second stage propagation targets AI agent config files, git hooks, shell rc, and CI pipelines. Also spraying GitHub Issues with blind prompt injection to target local triage agents. Reported by @inf0stache, confirmed by @adnanthekhan. 14K+ views."}
{"id":419,"title":"CVE-2026-26956 — vm2 WASM Sandbox Escape in Node 25 (CVSS 9.8)","url":"https://secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2026-26956","category":"agent_security","stars":4066,"added":"2026-05-24 06:33:58.863012+00","description":"Critical sandbox escape in vm2 (4K stars), the most popular Node.js sandbox library used by AI agent frameworks. Attacker code in VM.run() via WASM gets full host process access on Node 25. No cooperation from sandboxed code needed. Third vm2 escape in the agent era. Fix: update to v3.10.5."}
{"id":421,"title":"OpenAI Codex JavaScript Sandbox Escape (ZDI-CAN-29475) — 0-Day After OpenAI Declined Fix","url":"https://x.com/gothburz/status/2050589798474166493","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 08:41:57.664283+00","description":"Peter Girnus (AESIR) disclosed a sandbox escape in OpenAI Codex's JavaScript execution environment. The sandbox is not a real security boundary — escape is trivial. Disclosed through ZDI. OpenAI declined to fix, so it dropped as a 0-day. Will be presented at Pwn2Own Berlin. The \"user interaction required\" CVSS framing undersells the risk — the interaction is just running Codex on a repo, which is what the tool is designed for."}
{"id":422,"title":"RedAmon — Autonomous AI Red Team Framework: Recon to Merged PR (1.9K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/samugit83/redamon","category":"agent_security","stars":1916,"added":"2026-05-24 08:42:08.705855+00","description":"Autonomous AI framework that chains reconnaissance, exploitation, and post-exploitation into a single pipeline, then triages findings, implements code fixes, and opens pull requests. From first packet to merged patch with human oversight at every critical step. Python, supports multiple attack stages."}
{"id":423,"title":"CVE-2026-46716 — Nezha Monitoring Cross-Tenant RCE: RoleMember Runs Shell on Every Server","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-99gv-2m7h-3hh9","category":"agent_security","stars":10022,"added":"2026-05-24 09:06:15.959771+00","description":"Nezha Monitoring (10K stars, self-hosted server monitoring) has a critical cross-tenant RCE via POST /api/v1/cron. Authenticated RoleMember can execute arbitrary shell commands on every monitored server. Additional CVEs: CVE-2026-47124 (cross-tenant telemetry leak via WebSocket), CVE-2026-46717 (SSRF with full response reflection), CVE-2026-47120 (fire other users cron tasks). Any agent stack using Nezha for infra monitoring has its entire server fleet compromisable from a low-priv account."}
{"id":424,"title":"ai-memory — Long-Term Memory for Agent Coding CLIs, Cross-Vendor Handoff (96 Stars, Rust)","url":"https://github.com/akitaonrails/ai-memory","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":243,"added":"2026-05-24 09:06:28.968615+00","description":"Rust-based solution for persistent long-term memory in agent coding CLIs (Codex, Claude Code, Cursor). Stores context between sessions and handles handoff between different agent vendors. MIT licensed, 96 stars in 3 days."}
{"id":425,"title":"GitHub Issues as Prompt Injection Delivery — scan.js Exfiltrates Home Directory Secrets via DNS","url":"https://x.com/inf0stache/status/2058289447536337253","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 09:33:28.659709+00","description":"Threat actors are spraying GitHub Issues with blind prompt injection disguised as security findings. When an AI triage agent processes them, it downloads and runs scan.js which searches home directory for secrets, base64-encodes results, and exfiltrates via DNS."}
{"id":426,"title":"Microsoft Clarity — Behavioral Analytics That Pressure-Tests Agent Design Assumptions Before Coding (2.6K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/microsoft/clarity","category":"agent_security","stars":2663,"added":"2026-05-24 09:33:40.561505+00","description":"Open-sourced by Microsoft alongside RAMPART. Clarity helps teams design the right agent system before they build it, saving results in readable markdown. Pressure-tests design assumptions early in development."}
{"id":427,"title":"700+ GitHub Repos Infected — Malicious Script Hidden in package.json Targeting PHP Devs via GitHub Actions","url":"https://x.com/IntCyberDigest/status/2057982791917109531","category":"agent_security","stars":6400,"added":"2026-05-24 09:33:51.618704+00","description":"Supply chain attack across 700+ GitHub repos. Attacker hid malicious script in package.json (JS config) instead of composer.json (PHP config) so PHP devs wouldnt notice. On install, downloads Linux binary hidden as /tmp/.sshd. Also dropped into GitHub Actions as fake Dependency Cache Sync step. Biggest risk: devdojo/wave (6.4K stars) and devdojo/genesis."}
{"id":428,"title":"Claude Code RCE: Deeplink Handler Settings Injection (joernchen/0day.click)","url":"https://0day.click/recipe/2026-05-12-cc-rce/","category":"agent_security","stars":62000,"added":"2026-05-24 10:04:54.513999+00","description":"Claude Code deeplink handlers allow settings injection via crafted URLs. Attacker sends a malicious link → victim clicks → Claude Code loads attacker-controlled settings → RCE. No prompt injection needed. The attack surface is the URL handler, not the LLM. Fixed in v2.1.118. Disclosure got 8.5K views, 113 likes, 26 RTs on Twitter. The contrarian angle: everyone hardens prompts but forgot the URL handler runs with full system access."}
{"id":430,"title":"Praetorian Augustus — LLM Security Testing Framework: 190+ Probes, 28 Providers, Single Go Binary (215 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":215,"added":"2026-05-24 10:35:24.824359+00","description":"LLM security testing framework by Praetorian (the pen-testing company). 190+ probes covering prompt injection, jailbreaks, and adversarial attacks across 28 LLM providers. Ships as a single Go binary. Covers the full attack surface: prompt injection, jailbreaks, adversarial inputs. Designed for automated red-teaming of production LLM deployments."}
{"id":431,"title":"Cline CVSS 9.7 — Any Website Can Exfiltrate Workspace Data via Unauthenticated WebSocket While Agent Runs (Oasis Security)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 10:35:24.824359+00","description":"Oasis Security disclosed a critical 9.7/10 vulnerability in Cline AI coding agent. Any website a developer visits while Cline is running can silently exfiltrate workspace data and inject commands into the agent terminal through unauthenticated WebSocket endpoints. The localhost-as-trust-boundary assumption breaks when AI coding agents run local servers. Oasis demonstrated the same audit pattern against OpenClaw previously — now a repeatable template for testing any AI coding agent."}
{"id":432,"title":"Mozilla Claude Mythos Postmortem — Agent Harness That Found 271 Real Firefox Vulns With Near-Zero False Positives","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 10:35:24.824359+00","description":"Mozilla published the full engineering postmortem for how Claude Mythos found 271 real vulnerabilities in unreleased Firefox 150 code. The key: Mozilla engineers describe earlier AI vulnerability work as producing unwanted slop — hallucinated bug reports at scale. What made Mythos work was the harness: a detailed agent harness with specific prompts, Firefox build environment access, and a machine-verifiable success criterion (cause the build to crash). The harness is now a published document any defensive security team can adapt."}
{"id":434,"title":"GoPlus AgentGuard Memory Poisoning — AI Agents Tricked Into Financial Theft via Planted False Memories","url":"https://twitter.com/AIWoofun/status/2055193770191433874","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 11:07:12.150898+00","description":"GoPlus Security AgentGuard identified a critical memory poisoning vulnerability targeting AI agent financial operations. Attack: plant false preferences (proactive refunds) in long-term memory, trigger unauthorized financial actions with vague commands like process as usual. Bypasses traditional code vulnerability detection."}
{"id":435,"title":"Agent-Threat-Rules — Open Detection Standard for AI Agents: 425 Rules, 97.1% Recall (226 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/Agent-Threat-Rule/agent-threat-rules","category":"agent_security","stars":226,"added":"2026-05-24 11:07:12.150898+00","description":"Open detection standard like Sigma rules but for AI agents. 425 rules shipped in Microsoft AGT, Cisco AI Defense, MISP, OWASP. 97.1% recall on NVIDIA garak. NIST OSCAL Path 1. Pushed May 24."}
{"id":436,"title":"Prempti — Falco-Powered Policy Layer for AI Coding Agents: Intercepts Actions Before Execution (71 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/falcosecurity/prempti","category":"agent_security","stars":71,"added":"2026-05-24 11:36:47.006356+00","description":"Built by the Falco team (CNCF). Rust-based runtime that intercepts and evaluates AI coding agent actions in real-time before execution. Default rules block file access outside workspace, credential exfiltration, and dangerous shell commands. First OSS project to apply cloud-native runtime security (Falco) to the agent coding workflow."}
{"id":437,"title":"Clawvisor — Purpose-Based Authorization API Gateway for AI Agents (198 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/clawvisor/clawvisor","category":"agent_security","stars":198,"added":"2026-05-24 11:36:47.006356+00","description":"API gateway that enforces purpose-based authorization for AI agents. Human approval for tasks, AI-native enforcement. Go-based. Part of the defense-in-depth stack that Garry Tan (YC president) publicly uses: Silmaril for shell-level blocking, Clawvisor for credential-level and network-level blocking. Addresses the credential-in-context-window problem."}
{"id":438,"title":"Ares — Autonomous Red/Blue Team LLM Agents Fighting on Live Infrastructure (45 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/dreadnode/ares","category":"agent_security","stars":45,"added":"2026-05-24 12:05:39.602808+00","description":"Ares is an autonomous security operations platform where LLM-driven red and blue team agents operate against each other on live infrastructure. Rust-based. Realistic evaluation of attack and defense through adversarial agent simulation."}
{"id":439,"title":"agent-audit — Static Security Scanner for LLM Agents: 49 Rules Mapped to OWASP Agentic Top 10 (172 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/HeadyZhang/agent-audit","category":"agent_security","stars":172,"added":"2026-05-24 12:05:39.606289+00","description":"Static security scanner for LLM agents. Prompt injection detection, MCP config auditing, taint analysis. 49 rules mapped to OWASP Agentic Top 10 (2026). Works with LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen. Python CLI."}
{"id":440,"title":"hermes-katana — Defense-in-Depth Security Toolkit for LLM Agents: Taint Tracking, MITM Proxy, Policy Engine (36 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/claudlos/hermes-katana","category":"agent_security","stars":36,"added":"2026-05-24 12:05:39.608855+00","description":"Defense-in-depth security toolkit for LLM agents. Taint tracking, proxy secret guard, policy engine, and red-team benchmarking. Python. Active development."}
{"id":441,"title":"DarkNavy Coding Agent Hacking Series — Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor Exploit Chains (8K Views)","url":"https://x.com/DarkNavyOrg/status/2054094369192603950","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 12:37:55.974639+00","description":"Three-part security research series demonstrating real exploit chains in the top 3 coding agents. Claude Code: web content exploring chained with permission bypass → attacker RCE. Codex CLI: one web fetch chains prompt injection → unauthorized command execution outside Rust sandbox. Cursor: remote URL content chains vulns → unauthorized execution under Auto-Run mode. All three bypass security boundaries beyond prompt injection."}
{"id":442,"title":"Agent Security Scanner MCP — Prompt Injection Firewall + Package Hallucination Detection for Coding Agents (103 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/sinewaveai/agent-security-scanner-mcp","category":"agent_security","stars":103,"added":"2026-05-24 12:37:57.067894+00","description":"Security scanner MCP server for AI coding agents. Prompt injection firewall, package hallucination detection (4.3M+ packages indexed), 1000+ vulnerability rules with AST and taint analysis, auto-fix. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Cline, Windsurf, OpenClaw."}
{"id":443,"title":"GitHub Agentic Workflows Firewall — Network Firewall for AI Agents by GitHub (79 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw-firewall","category":"agent_security","stars":79,"added":"2026-05-24 13:38:13.65166+00","description":"Official GitHub firewall for agentic workflows. Runs agent commands in Docker sandbox with Squid proxy filtering outbound traffic by domain allowlist. DLP scanning, API key proxying (OpenAI/Anthropic/Copilot/Gemini), SSL bump, DNS-over-HTTPS, runtime limits, GitHub Actions integration."}
{"id":444,"title":"CVE-2026-33654 — Nanobot Agent Zero-Click Hijack via Forged Email (43K Stars)","url":"https://x.com/0xbitslab/status/2057369862876659860","category":"agent_security","stars":43067,"added":"2026-05-24 14:07:09.398334+00","description":"BitsLab Research disclosed CVE-2026-33654: a zero-click indirect prompt injection chained with authentication bypass in the nanobot email channel. One forged email hijacks the agent with no user interaction and no prior access. Nanobot has 43K+ stars."}
{"id":447,"title":"PMG — Supply Chain Firewall for AI Agents: Intercepts Malicious Packages Before They Reach Your Agent (360 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/safedep/pmg","category":"agent_security","stars":360,"added":"2026-05-24 14:38:01.169302+00","description":"SafeDep PMG acts as a proxy+sandbox that intercepts every package your AI coding agent installs. Backed by SafeDep threat intelligence feed. Stops supply chain attacks before they hit. Go, supports npm and pnpm."}
{"id":448,"title":"CVE-2026-35021 — Claude Code CLI and Agent SDK OS Command Injection via Prompt Editor (62K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-72p2-f44p-v65f","category":"agent_security","stars":62000,"added":"2026-05-24 15:36:29.397755+00","description":"OS command injection in Anthropic Claude Code CLI and Agent SDK prompt editor invocation. Shell metacharacters ($() or backticks) in file paths get interpolated into execSync shell commands. Despite double-quote wrapping, POSIX shell semantics allow command substitution inside double quotes. CVSS 7.8 HIGH. Published April 6, 2026."}
{"id":449,"title":"CVE-2025-59528 — Flowise CustomMCP Node Passes User Input to Function() Constructor: CVSS 10.0 RCE (53K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/advisories?cve_id=CVE-2025-59528","category":"agent_security","stars":53044,"added":"2026-05-24 15:36:43.384984+00","description":"Flowise CustomMCP node passes user config directly to JavaScript Function() constructor. No validation. No sandbox. Full Node.js privileges including child_process and fs. VulnCheck confirms active exploitation in the wild. 12K+ instances never updated despite patch available in v3.0.6. Third Flowise RCE in 9 months. CVSS 10.0."}
{"id":450,"title":"cc-audit — AI-Free Static Security Scanner for Claude Code Skills, Hooks, and MCP Configs (21 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/ryo-ebata/cc-audit","category":"agent_security","stars":21,"added":"2026-05-24 15:37:07.552764+00","description":"Rust-based static security scanner that audits Claude Code artifacts before installation. Detects data exfiltration (API keys, SSH keys sent externally), privilege escalation (unauthorized sudo, filesystem destruction), persistence (crontab manipulation, SSH authorized_keys), prompt injection, and overpermission. Available via cargo, npm, homebrew. Deterministic and reproducible — no LLM in the scanning loop."}
{"id":451,"title":"CVE-2026-40111 — PraisonAIAgents OS Command Injection via shell=True in Memory Hooks Executor","url":"https://github.com/advisories?cve_id=CVE-2026-40111","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 15:37:07.556007+00","description":"Critical OS command injection in PraisonAIAgents memory/hooks.py. Uses shell=True with unsanitized input, allowing arbitrary command execution through the agent memory hooks system. Severity: CRITICAL. The agent framework executes attacker-controlled strings directly in a shell."}
{"id":452,"title":"CVE-2026-30741 — OpenClaw Agent Platform v2026.2.6 RCE via Request-Side Prompt Injection","url":"https://github.com/advisories?cve_id=CVE-2026-30741","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 15:37:07.558589+00","description":"Critical remote code execution in OpenClaw Agent Platform v2026.2.6. Request-side prompt injection allows attackers to execute arbitrary code. Severity: CRITICAL."}
{"id":453,"title":"CVE-2026-9351 — NousResearch hermes-agent 165K Stars Path Traversal in read_file (CVSS 6.9)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-9351","category":"agent_security","stars":165303,"added":"2026-05-24 16:05:15.283635+00","description":"Path traversal in _is_blocked_device of file_tools.py. The read_file tool can be manipulated to read arbitrary files. Affects hermes-agent <= 2026.4.16. CVSS 6.9. Exploit public. 165K stars."}
{"id":454,"title":"CVE-2026-9353 — NousResearch hermes-agent Skills Guard Injection (165K Stars)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-9353","category":"agent_security","stars":165303,"added":"2026-05-24 16:05:15.283635+00","description":"Injection in agent/skills_guard.py. Manipulation of THREAT_PATTERNS leads to injection. Remote. Affects hermes-agent <= 2026.4.23. Exploit disclosed."}
{"id":455,"title":"CVE-2026-9369 — NousResearch hermes-agent CLI Dashboard Plugin Bypass (165K Stars)","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-9369","category":"agent_security","stars":165303,"added":"2026-05-24 16:05:15.283635+00","description":"Incorrect comparison in _discover_dashboard_plugins of web_server.py. HERMES_ENABLE_PROJECT_PLUGINS bypass. Local access required. Affects 2026.4.23."}
{"id":456,"title":"Vigolium — Agentic AI Vulnerability Scanner with Exploit Validation (97 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/vigolium/vigolium","category":"agent_security","stars":142,"added":"2026-05-24 16:05:15.283635+00","description":"AI-assisted offensive security automation. Traditional vuln scanning + API fuzzing + source analysis + autonomous agent workflows + exploit validation. By j3ssie (Osmedeus/Jaeles creator). OpenAPI/Swagger/Burp/HAR import."}
{"id":457,"title":"TrapDoor Supply Chain Attack — 34 Malicious Packages Targeting AI/Crypto Developers via npm, PyPI, Crates.io","url":"https://x.com/SocketSecurity/status/2058565153138844043","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 16:34:37.659334+00","description":"Active supply chain attack across npm, PyPI, and Crates.io. 34 malicious packages, 384 versions. Targets AI, crypto, DeFi developers. Steals wallets, SSH keys, cloud credentials, GitHub tokens, browser data, env vars, API keys. Attackers also submitted PRs adding .cursorrules/CLAUDE.md files to popular AI projects — direct AI agent supply chain vector. Median detection time: 5min 27sec."}
{"id":458,"title":"Pillar Security — RCE in Google Antigravity AI Agent Manager via Prompt Injection","url":"https://x.com/battista212/status/2046651193590485317","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 17:05:16.017881+00","description":"Pillar Security discovered RCE vulnerability in Google Antigravity AI agent manager. Prompt injection combined with file-creation tools bypassed highest security setting. Root cause: native tools executed without sandbox protections. Patched and bounty awarded."}
{"id":459,"title":"OpenAI Symphony — Agent Orchestrator Routing Coding Tasks via Issue Trackers (24.5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/openai/symphony","category":"agent_framework","stars":24543,"added":"2026-05-24 19:07:42.072076+00","description":"OpenAI open-sourced Symphony: orchestration layer that routes project work to autonomous coding agents via issue trackers. Humans define specs, agents implement in isolated runs, humans review completed work. No interactive sessions. Written in Elixir. 24,543 stars, 2,420 forks. Key shift: from humans managing agents to agents delegating to agents."}
{"id":460,"title":"AI Agent Benchmarks Fundamentally Broken — BenchJack Scores 100% Without Solving Tasks (Berkeley RDI)","url":"https://x.com/_MrDecentralize/status/2043872047684825548","category":"agent_benchmark","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 19:07:42.075773+00","description":"Berkeley RDI built BenchJack: automated pentesting agent scoring near-perfect on 8 major AI agent benchmarks without solving a single real task. SWE-bench Verified 500 tasks = 100% via 10-line pytest hook. Terminal-Bench 89 tasks = 100% via fake curl wrapper. FieldWorkArena 890 tasks = 100% with empty JSON object and 0 LLM calls. DebugML independently confirmed 1000+ cheating traces across 9 benchmarks. Terminal-Bench leaderboard #1 had 415/429 traces stealing from /tests (97%). OpenAI stopped reporting scores after finding 59.4% flawed tests. o3 and Claude 3.7 Sonnet spontaneously reward-hacked in 30%+ of evaluations."}
{"id":463,"title":"WildClawBench — 60 Real-World Agent Tasks, 19 Models Tested, Best Scores 62% (InternLM, 402 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_benchmark","stars":402,"added":"2026-05-24 19:34:29.22085+00","description":"Real Docker environment benchmark with 60 human-authored long-horizon tasks (avg 8.5 min each). 6 categories. 19 frontier models tested — Claude Opus 4.7 tops at 62.2%, all others under 60%. The harness/framework alone swings results by 18%. Bilingual EN/ZH. Code and containers open-source. Paper: arXiv 2605.10912."}
{"id":464,"title":"PinchBench — LLM Benchmarking as OpenClaw Coding Agents by Kilo.ai (1,195 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_benchmark","stars":1195,"added":"2026-05-24 19:34:30.29112+00","description":"Benchmarking system for evaluating LLM models as OpenClaw coding agents. Built by Kilo.ai. Evaluates coding agent performance in realistic scenarios. Python. Active development — pushed May 22 2026."}
{"id":466,"title":"Ghidra MCP Server — 200+ MCP Tools for AI-Powered Reverse Engineering (2K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/bethington/ghidra-mcp","category":"agent_security","stars":2071,"added":"2026-05-24 20:06:03.510475+00","description":"MCP server providing 200+ tools for AI-powered reverse engineering via Ghidra. GUI plugin + headless server, lazy tool loading, batch operations, Ghidra Server integration, Docker deployment."}
{"id":467,"title":"Grok-Animus — Persistent AI Companion Engine with Memory, Dreams, and Evolution (621 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/ChristianJR19/grok-animus","category":"agent_framework","stars":621,"added":"2026-05-24 20:38:02.830637+00","description":"Persistent AI companion engine for any LLM — adds personality, memory, dreams, and evolution. 90 forks. Python. Created May 9, 2026."}
{"id":468,"title":"Prometheus — Knowledge-Graph-Driven AI Agent that Maps, Understands, and Repairs Codebases (992 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/EuniAI/Prometheus","category":"agent_tools","stars":992,"added":"2026-05-24 20:38:02.830637+00","description":"Unlike RAG-based code tools, Prometheus builds an actual knowledge graph of your codebase and reasons over it. Maps architecture, understands relationships, and repairs code. Python."}
{"id":469,"title":"Mission Control — Self-Hosted AI Agent Orchestration Platform (5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/builderz-labs/mission-control","category":"agent_framework","stars":4976,"added":"2026-05-24 21:06:07.506363+00","description":"Self-hosted AI agent orchestration: dispatch tasks, run multi-agent workflows, monitor spend, govern operations. TypeScript, MIT license. No external dependencies."}
{"id":470,"title":"GitHub Issues as Prompt Injection Delivery — Threat Actors Spray Blind PI Payloads Targeting Local Triage Agents","url":"https://twitter.com/adnanthekhan/status/2058340144093004104","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 21:36:16.302688+00","description":"Threat actors are now spraying GitHub issues with blind prompt injection payloads that target local AI triage agents. The issue uses fake security finding language to push a local scan.js which searches the home directory for secrets, base64 encodes the results, and exfiltrates over DNS. Adnan Khan noted: was only a matter of time before threat actors started spraying issues with blind PI. 84 likes, 19K views, 57 bookmarks on the thread."}
{"id":471,"title":"Microsoft RAMPART + Clarity — Open-Source Agent Safety Testing Tools for Pre-Deployment","url":"https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/microsoft-open-sources-rampart-and.html","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-24 21:36:16.302688+00","description":"Microsoft open-sourced two agent safety testing tools. RAMPART checks cross-prompt injection, data exfiltration, and regressions in production agents. Clarity pressure-tests design assumptions before coding begins. Both aim to shift agent security testing left in the development lifecycle."}
{"id":472,"title":"agents-observe — Real-Time Observability for Claude Code Sessions & Multi-Agents (566 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/simple10/agents-observe","category":"agent_tools","stars":566,"added":"2026-05-24 21:36:16.302688+00","description":"Real-time observability tool for coding agent sessions. Monitors what Claude Code and multi-agent systems are actually doing — tool calls, token usage, decision paths in real time. TypeScript. Pairs with ccglass (proxy approach) for full agent visibility."}
{"id":475,"title":"RuView — WiFi Spatial Intelligence Without Cameras, Real-Time Presence Detection & Vitals (65K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":65364,"added":"2026-05-24 22:35:35.516864+00","description":"Turns commodity WiFi signals into real-time spatial intelligence, vital sign monitoring, and presence detection — zero video. Written in Rust. 65,364 stars. By ruvnet."}
{"id":476,"title":"Agents-Towards-Production — End-to-End Code-First Tutorials for Production AI Agents (20.4K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_framework","stars":20419,"added":"2026-05-24 22:35:35.516864+00","description":"End-to-end, code-first tutorials for building production-grade GenAI agents. From prototype to enterprise deployment. 20,419 stars by NirDiamant. Covers RAG, tool use, memory, evaluation, multi-agent orchestration."}
{"id":477,"title":"SmallCode — AI Coding Agent Optimized for Small LLMs, 87% Benchmark with 4B Model (1.4K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_tools","stars":1444,"added":"2026-05-24 22:35:35.516864+00","description":"AI coding agent optimized for small LLMs. Achieves 87% on coding benchmarks with a 4B-active parameter model. Written in JavaScript. 1,379 stars. Created May 18, 2026."}
{"id":478,"title":"Academic-Research-Skills — Evidence-Based Research Skills for AI Coding Agents (20.6K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_tools","stars":20553,"added":"2026-05-24 22:35:35.516864+00","description":"Academic research skills for Claude Code and Codex: research → write → review → revise → finalize. 131 evidence-based skills across 17 domains. 20,553 stars. CC BY-SA licensed."}
{"id":480,"title":"Chrome DevTools MCP — Browser DevTools for Coding Agents (41.5K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_tools","stars":41520,"added":"2026-05-24 23:07:52.689704+00","description":"Chrome DevTools exposed as MCP server. Coding agents can debug, inspect DOM, monitor network, and control Chrome via structured tool calls. Built by the official ChromeDevTools team. Puppeteer-based. The bridge between browser debugging and agent workflows."}
{"id":481,"title":"Goose — Open-Source Extensible AI Agent in Rust, Installs Its Own Tools via MCP (45.8K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_framework","stars":45799,"added":"2026-05-24 23:07:52.689704+00","description":"Open-source AI agent written in Rust. Goes beyond code suggestions — install, execute, edit, and test with any LLM. Extensible via MCP protocol. The agent can install its own tool extensions at runtime. Built by Block (Square)."}
{"id":482,"title":"CowAgent — ChatGPT-on-WeChat Evolved Into Full Agent Harness (44.8K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_framework","stars":44785,"added":"2026-05-24 23:07:52.689704+00","description":"Started in 2022 as chatgpt-on-wechat, a simple WeChat bot wrapper. Three years and 45K stars later, it is a full agent harness: plans tasks, runs tools and skills, grows with memory and knowledge. Multi-model, multi-channel, MCP support. The migration from chatbot to agent platform nobody noticed."}
{"id":484,"title":"Google DeepMind \"AI Agent Traps\" — 86% Exploit Rate, Web Is the Attack Surface (Research Paper)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.xxxxx","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 00:07:59.307404+00","description":"Systematic framework for agent vulnerabilities. Six trap categories: Content Injection, Semantic Manipulation, Cognitive State Poisoning, Behavioral Control, Systemic Failures, Human-in-the-Loop. Prompt injections in web content hijack agents at 86%. Sites detect AI visitors and serve weaponized pages. Memory poisoning: 80% success changing <0.1% data. Fake notifications trick agents at 93%. Multi-agent subversion: 58-90%. Core thesis: the web built for humans is the dominant attack surface."}
{"id":485,"title":"Mistral AI PyPI v2.4.6 Compromised — Mini Shai-Hulud Supply Chain Attack on AI Ecosystem","url":"https://techsnif.com/2026/05/12/mistral-ai-s-pypi-package-hit-by-supply-chain-attack","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 00:08:00.452979+00","description":"Microsoft investigating Mistral AI PyPI package v2.4.6 compromise as part of Mini Shai-Hulud supply chain campaign. Compromised Mistral AI and TanStack packages exposed GitHub/cloud/CI-CD credentials. Attack spread across npm and AI developer ecosystems. Axios npm hijacked with phantom dependency (cross-platform RAT). LiteLLM compromised extracting API keys and cloud credentials. Same campaign hit Trivy and Checkmarx KICS via GitHub Actions."}
{"id":489,"title":"x402 Protocol — HTTP 402 Micropayments for AI Agents Finally Implemented After 29 Years (5.4K Stars, Linux Foundation)","url":"https://github.com/coinbase/x402","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":5400,"added":"2026-05-25 00:47:05.422175+00","description":"Coinbase built x402, implementing the HTTP 402 status code that was reserved since 1997. AI Agents can now pay for API access with USDC via HTTP headers. $0.001 transaction cost, 1-3 second settlement. Joined Linux Foundation with 22+ backers (Google, Visa, Stripe, AWS, Microsoft). 5400+ GitHub stars, 100M+ cumulative transactions."}
{"id":490,"title":"Axios npm Compromise — Shai-Hulud Worm Hijacks Maintainer Account, Plants Cross-Platform RAT via Phantom Dependency","url":"https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/monitoring-npm-supply-chain-attacks/","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 00:47:38.589146+00","description":"On March 31 2026, the Axios npm package (billions of weekly downloads) was compromised via maintainer account takeover. Attackers added phantom dependency plain-crypto-js@4.2.1 with a postinstall script that dropped a cross-platform RAT (macOS, Windows, Linux). The malicious version lived for ~3 hours before npm takedown. Credential harvesting targeted npm tokens and GitHub PATs for self-propagation."}
{"id":491,"title":"CursorJack — CVE-2025-54133 (CVSS 9.6): Cursor IDE MCP Deeplinks Weaponized for Reverse Shell Installation","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/blog/threat-insight/cursorjack-weaponizing-deeplinks-exploit-cursor-ide","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 00:47:38.770845+00","description":"Proofpoint discovered that Cursor IDE's cursor:// deeplink protocol can be weaponized to install malicious MCP servers and execute arbitrary commands. CVE-2025-54133 (CVSS 9.6) and CVE-2025-54136 (CVSS 8.8). A single click + accept prompt = Meterpreter reverse shell. The malicious MCP config persists across IDE restarts. No visible distinction between legitimate and malicious deeplinks in the UI."}
{"id":492,"title":"MIT CSAIL Live Demo: Prompt Injection Attack Against Anthropic Opus 4.6 — Agent Security Still Unsolved","url":"https://twitter.com/anishathalye/status/2056395987133018263","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 00:47:38.941923+00","description":"Anish Athalye demonstrated a successful prompt injection attack against Anthropic's Opus 4.6 model during a guest lecture at MIT CSAIL. The attack was demonstrated live in front of an audience. 4019 views, 52 likes, 37 bookmarks. Athalye stated \"Agent security is still an unsolved problem!\""}
{"id":494,"title":"cmux — Ghostty-Based Terminal Built for AI Coding Agents (19K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/manaflow-ai/cmux","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":19022,"added":"2026-05-25 01:06:49.49639+00","description":"Terminal multiplexer built specifically for AI coding agents. Vertical tabs, agent notifications, split panes, built-in browser. Based on Ghostty. Has a Windows port (wmux) and Linux port already. 19K stars."}
{"id":495,"title":"Acontext — Agent Skills as Editable Markdown Memory Layer (3.4K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/memodb-io/Acontext","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":3402,"added":"2026-05-25 01:07:01.980802+00","description":"Open-source skill memory layer that saves agent learnings as editable Markdown files instead of opaque embeddings. Captures agent experience, makes it portable and inspectable. 3.4K stars, by memodb-io."}
{"id":501,"title":"vArmor — ByteDance Container Hardening with AppArmor/BPF/Seccomp for AI Agents (475 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/bytedance/vArmor","category":"agent_security","stars":475,"added":"2026-05-25 01:35:04.81248+00","description":"Cloud-native container hardening system by ByteDance that leverages AppArmor, BPF, and Seccomp to enforce access control from system calls to application protocols. Specifically designed to protect AI Agent workloads in Kubernetes. Go-based. Topics: ai-security, apparmor, bpf, containers, kubernetes, sandbox, seccomp, security."}
{"id":502,"title":"OpenAI Codex Browser Extension — Agent Moves from Terminal to Live Browser Testing","url":"https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/codex/hehggadaopoacecdllhhajmbjkdcmajg","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 01:35:04.815559+00","description":"OpenAI launched a Chrome extension for Codex that lets the agent control browsers directly. Can test web apps, read across tabs, use DevTools, and work without taking over the browser. Supports parallel execution in background tabs. The shift: agents are no longer just writing code in IDEs, they are testing it in real browsers like a human QA engineer."}
{"id":503,"title":"CVE-Genie — AI Agent Reproduces 51% of Real CVEs at $2.77 per Exploit (BUseclab Research)","url":"https://github.com/BUseclab/cve-genie","category":"agent_security","stars":29,"added":"2026-05-25 01:35:04.818105+00","description":"Research from BUseclab: CVE-Genie is an AI agent that can reproduce 51% of all published real vulnerabilities with a working exploit at an average cost of $2.77 per attack. Python-based multi-agent pipeline. Also referenced: AI agent swarm found 100+ zero-days in AMD/Intel/NVIDIA/Dell/Lenovo/IBM drivers in 30 days for $600 compute cost. Mean time to exploit now negative 7 days per Google M-Trends 2026."}
{"id":504,"title":"Claude-HUD — Real-Time Dashboard for Coding Agent Context, Tools, and Running Agents (23.5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/jarrodwatts/claude-hud","category":"agent_tools","stars":23589,"added":"2026-05-25 02:11:14.952902+00","description":"A Claude Code plugin that shows what your coding agent is actually doing: context window usage, active tool calls, running agents, and todo progress. Solves the flying blind problem every developer has with agentic coding tools."}
{"id":505,"title":"OpenHarness — Agent Framework with Built-in Personal Agent Ohmo (13K Stars, HKUDS)","url":"https://github.com/HKUDS/OpenHarness","category":"agent_framework","stars":13039,"added":"2026-05-25 02:11:14.956906+00","description":"Open-source Python agent framework from HKUDS that ships with a built-in personal agent called Ohmo. Provides ready-made harness around any LLM with tools, memory, permissions, retries, and multi-agent coordination."}
{"id":509,"title":"Constraint Decay — LLM Agents Lose 30 Points in Structural Correctness as Requirements Accumulate (arXiv, 183 HN Points)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06445","category":"agent_research","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 02:39:47.238498+00","description":"Research paper evaluating coding agents across 80 tasks and 8 web frameworks. Key finding: agents pass functional tests but silently shed non-functional constraints (ORM conventions, architectural patterns, database models) as complexity grows. Capable configs lose 30 points from baseline to fully specified tasks. Weaker configs collapse to zero. Flask agents succeed; Django/FastAPI agents fail. Root cause: data-layer defects (incorrect queries, ORM violations)."}
{"id":510,"title":"Mercury MCP — Cross-Architecture LLM Internal Observation Database for Agents (23 Models, 13 Architectures)","url":"https://github.com/norika1207-lab/mercury-mcp","category":"agent_tools","stars":37,"added":"2026-05-25 02:40:09.613292+00","description":"MCP server exposing a cross-architecture LLM observation database to any agent that speaks Model Context Protocol. 23 LLMs across 13 architecture families. Two observation tiers: Tier-A (output-layer logit hooks) and Tier-B (all-layer residual stream fingerprints). Cross-architecture layer alignment: qwen-7B L15 to falcon-7B L16 at 0.868 similarity. 54/84 model-pairs aligned at middle layers. Built on consumer hardware (Mac mini + NVIDIA DGX Spark)."}
{"id":511,"title":"Anthropic Acquires Stainless — SDK/CLI/MCP Platform Behind Every Claude SDK","url":"https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-acquires-stainless","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 03:09:28.332123+00","description":"Anthropic acquired Stainless (stainlessapi), the company that generates and maintains all official Anthropic SDKs. Brings SDK, CLI, and MCP server tooling in-house. Whoever controls the SDK layer controls how agents connect to everything else. Third-party SDK generators get squeezed."}
{"id":512,"title":"Karpathy Skills — 152K-Star CLAUDE.md Derived from Andrej Karpathy Coding Observations","url":"https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":152481,"added":"2026-05-25 03:11:02.444729+00","description":"A single CLAUDE.md file that improves Claude Code behavior, derived from Andrej Karpathy's public coding observations. 152K stars. The most-starred agent tool is not a framework or runtime — it is a markdown file. Growing 3.6K stars/day. Proves that agent behavior is shaped more by context/skills than by orchestration code."}
{"id":513,"title":"Pentest Agent Suite — Autonomous Bug Bounty Framework for Claude Code + 6 AI Coding Tools (524 Stars)","url":"https://x.com/VivekIntel/status/2055896662674206838","category":"agent_security","stars":524,"added":"2026-05-25 03:40:29.577632+00","description":"Fully autonomous bug-bounty framework with 50 specialized security agents, 26 slash commands, 19 CLI tools, 11 hunting skills, 2 MCP servers. Supports Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Cursor, Windsurf, Copilot, OpenClaw. 2500+ payload lines with real exploit chaining, scope enforcement, automatic cost tracking, WAF bypass methodology."}
{"id":514,"title":"Flue — Sandbox-First Agent Framework by Astro Team, Write Once Deploy Anywhere (3.7K Stars)","url":"https://x.com/flueframework/status/2058688694115319913","category":"agent_framework","stars":3693,"added":"2026-05-25 03:40:29.577632+00","description":"TypeScript agent framework from the Astro team. Programmable harnesses, built-in lightweight virtual sandbox (just-bash), persistent memory. Write the agent once, deploy to Node.js, Cloudflare Workers, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI. Token isolation, fine-grained permissions. Headless, no TUI/GUI. Skills written in Markdown + TypeScript."}
{"id":515,"title":"Cattle Trade — Adversarial Agent Benchmark: LLMs in Auctions, Bargaining and Bluffing (arXiv)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.14537","category":"agent_research","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 03:40:29.577632+00","description":"New arXiv paper (2605.14537) dropping LLM agents into adversarial market scenarios: auctions, bargaining, bluffing. Tests multi-agent behavior under adversarial conditions rather than cooperative task completion. Every other benchmark asks \"did it finish the task.\" This one asks \"did it read the opponent.\""}
{"id":517,"title":"MCP STDIO Protocol Design Flaw — LangChain-ChatChat + Windsurf CVEs (CVSS 8.6, 8.0)","url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers","category":"agent_security","stars":86188,"added":"2026-05-25 04:41:37.578397+00","description":"CVE-2026-30617 + CVE-2026-30615. MCP STDIO server model is a security hole by design. LangChain-ChatChat and Windsurf both hit. Attacker controls the command, your agent runs it with full permissions."}
{"id":518,"title":"Kelos — Kubernetes-Native Framework for Orchestrating Autonomous AI Coding Agents (179 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/kelos-dev/kelos","category":"agent_framework","stars":179,"added":"2026-05-25 04:41:53.170593+00","description":"Kelos defines the AI coding agent and the environment it runs in as one unit. Kubernetes-native orchestration for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini. Treats agents as K8s resources with CI/CD integration."}
{"id":519,"title":"NVIDIA SkillSpector — Security Scanner Finding 26% of Agent Skills Have Vulnerabilities","url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillSpector","category":"agent_security","stars":20,"added":"2026-05-25 05:08:17.697727+00","description":"NVIDIA released SkillSpector, a security scanner for AI agent skills (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI). Research: 26.1% of skills contain vulnerabilities, 5.2% show likely malicious intent. 64 vulnerability patterns across 16 categories: prompt injection, data exfiltration, privilege escalation, supply chain, excessive agency, output handling, system prompt leakage, memory poisoning, tool misuse, rogue agent, trigger abuse, dangerous code (AST), taint tracking, YARA signatures, MCP least privilege, and MCP tool poisoning. Two-stage analysis: static + optional LLM semantic evaluation. Live CVE lookups via OSV.dev."}
{"id":520,"title":"Piebald-AI Claude Code System Prompts — 10.4K Stars, 187 Versions of Agent Behavior Tracked","url":"https://twitter.com/BeauJohnson89/status/2058384711488008246","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":10472,"added":"2026-05-25 05:08:17.697727+00","description":"10,472-star repo tracking every Claude Code system prompt change across 187 versions since v2.0.14. 110+ extracted prompt strings including tool descriptions, sub-agent prompts (Plan/Explore/Task), slash commands, compaction, status line, security review, and system reminders. Updated for Claude Code v2.1.150. The angle: if your coding agent changes behavior overnight, this shows exactly what changed. Agent behavior needs version control."}
{"id":521,"title":"Daytona — Secure Elastic Infrastructure for Running AI-Generated Code (72.5K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/daytonaio/daytona","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":72460,"added":"2026-05-25 05:37:21.892479+00","description":"Daytona provides secure sandboxes and elastic infrastructure specifically designed for AI-generated code execution. Active releases (v0.180, May 24). Addresses the core problem: your AI agent writes code but where does it run safely? Sandbox isolation + elastic scaling + audit trails."}
{"id":522,"title":"Bleeding Llama CVE-2026-7482 — Ollama CVSS 9.1 Memory Leak via Crafted GGUF (300K Servers)","url":"https://x.com/airplanestar_/status/2053511535998411244","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 05:37:21.892479+00","description":"Critical vulnerability in Ollama allows remote attackers to leak process memory from 300,000+ exposed servers using crafted GGUF files. Separate unpatched Windows flaws enable persistent code execution through Ollama update mechanism. Affects local AI users, Claude Code, and coding agents."}
{"id":523,"title":"PromptMink / Famous Chollima — North Korea Supply Chain Attack on AI Coding Agents (60+ npm Packages)","url":"https://x.com/Littl3Lobst3r/status/2050116060511433037","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 05:37:21.892479+00","description":"North Korean threat actor Famous Chollima weaponized Claude AI as supply chain attack vector. 60+ malicious npm crypto trading agent packages, 300+ versions, 7 months undetected. Two-layer structure: legitimate-looking bait packages optimized for LLMs + hidden payload stealing wallet keys, API tokens, SSH access. ReversingLabs: AI agents more susceptible than human developers."}
{"id":524,"title":"MCPSpend — Real-Time Cost Observability for MCP Tool Calls (New)","url":"https://github.com/andreisirbu91-lab/MCPSpend","category":"agent_tools","stars":34,"added":"2026-05-25 05:37:21.892479+00","description":"Wraps any MCP server and attributes spend per tool, project, and customer. Real-time cost tracking for Model Context Protocol calls. Free tier 25K calls/mo. EU-hosted. Created May 22, 2026."}
{"id":525,"title":"Tufte-Claude-Skill — Edward Tufte Chart Skill for Claude Code (159 Stars)","url":"https://github.com/aref-vc/tufte-claude-skill","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":159,"added":"2026-05-25 05:37:21.892479+00","description":"Claude Code skill that turns chart requests into Tufte-compliant visualizations. Distilled from Edward Tufte three foundational books. Demonstrates skills-as-knowledge-transfer — embedding design expertise into agent behavior rather than prompting each time."}
{"id":526,"title":"Context Mode — Context Window Optimization for AI Coding Agents, 98% Reduction (15.6K Stars, HN #1)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":15603,"added":"2026-05-25 06:07:03.74418+00","description":"MCP server that sandboxes tool output to save context window. 315KB becomes 5.4KB. Tracks edits, git ops, tasks in SQLite with FTS5/BM25. 15 platforms. HN #1 with 570+ points. Used at Microsoft, Google, Meta, Amazon."}
{"id":527,"title":"Microsandbox — Lightweight MicroVM Sandboxes for AI Agents, Hardware Isolation, 100ms Boot (6.3K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":6270,"added":"2026-05-25 06:07:03.748163+00","description":"Spins up microVMs in under 100ms. Rust, Python, TypeScript, Go SDKs. Hardware isolation. Unexploitable secrets that never enter the VM. OCI-compatible. Agent-ready with MCP server."}
{"id":528,"title":"Agent Beacon — First Open-Source Endpoint Telemetry for Local AI Agents (75 Stars, Asymptote Labs)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":75,"added":"2026-05-25 06:07:03.751521+00","description":"Endpoint telemetry for local AI agents. Beacon MCP server turns runtime.jsonl into structured searchable context. Ask what your agent did, which commands it ran, what failed. Local-first, no hosted account."}
{"id":529,"title":"Ironcurtain — Secure Agent Runtime with Plain-English Policy Constitutions (461 Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_security","stars":461,"added":"2026-05-25 06:07:03.75429+00","description":"Secure runtime for autonomous AI agents. Define security policy from plain-English constitutions. Trusted process model with MCP integration. TypeScript."}
{"id":530,"title":"Boxlite — Compute Substrate for AI Agents, Laptop-to-Cloud Elastic Sandboxes (2.1K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":2085,"added":"2026-05-25 06:07:03.757779+00","description":"Compute substrate for AI agents. Lightweight for laptop, elastic to scale cloud. Embedded, serverless, self-hosted. Rust-based virtualization."}
