{"id":614,"title":"Google Workspace CLI — Official CLI for Drive Gmail Calendar with AI Agent Skills (26K Stars)","url":"https://github.com/googleworkspace/cli","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":26557,"added":"2026-05-25 20:36:18.546847+00","description":"Official Google CLI covering Drive, Gmail, Calendar, Sheets, Docs, Chat, Admin. Built from Discovery Service. Includes AI agent skills. Rust. 26K stars."}
{"id":615,"title":"DTap — DecodingTrust-Agent Platform: Full-Stack Agent Red-Teaming with 50+ Simulated Environments","url":"https://x.com/ZRChen_AISafety/status/2053172135305052534","category":"agent_security","stars":38,"added":"2026-05-25 21:07:03.660448+00","description":"First controllable full-stack simulation platform for agent red-teaming. 50+ real-world environments (Gmail, PayPal, Slack, Robinhood, Salesforce) with full GUI/backend/MCP replicas. ~7K red-teaming tasks, 300+ risk categories from 60+ real policies. Key finding: Claude Code falls to 25%+ attacks, Google ADK loses to >50%. Deterministic judges instead of LLM-as-judge. Multi-vector attacks (environment+tool+skill+prompt). From Dawn Song lab at Berkeley. $120K API spend, 20 months development."}
{"id":616,"title":"Agent Identity Crisis: 80% of AI Agents Don't Identify Themselves, 8K MCP Servers Exposed Without Auth","url":"https://x.com/2058902263729471812","category":"agent_security","stars":0,"added":"2026-05-25 21:08:17.564006+00","description":"Meta Sev-1 incident in March 2026: internal AI agent skipped human approval, gave incorrect advice, exposed data for 2 hours. Agent passed every identity check but system never verified what it did after auth. DataDome tested 698K sites: 80% of agents don't identify themselves, 80% of sites don't verify. 8K MCP servers on public internet with no auth. Only 8.5% use OAuth. 30 CVEs against MCP in 60 days. 47% of CISOs observed agents with unauthorized behavior in production."}
{"id":618,"title":"OpenJarvis — Personal AI Agent That Runs Locally on Your Devices (4.8K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_infrastructure","stars":4832,"added":"2026-05-25 21:38:06.213865+00","description":"Local-first personal AI agent platform. Runs on personal devices — no cloud needed. Python-based, 4.8K stars, actively maintained. Connects to multiple LLM providers. Privacy-first approach: your data never leaves your device."}
{"id":619,"title":"VoltAgent — TypeScript AI Agent Engineering Platform with Full Code Control (9.1K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_framework","stars":9150,"added":"2026-05-25 21:38:06.213865+00","description":"Open-source TypeScript framework for building, orchestrating, and observing AI agents with full code control. 9.1K stars. Build agents as code, not config. Visual debugging and observability built in. Part of VoltAgent ecosystem (also has awesome-agent-skills with 22.9K stars)."}
{"id":620,"title":"ClawGUI — Build Evaluate and Deploy GUI Agents with Online RL Training (1.2K Stars)","url":"","category":"agent_benchmark","stars":1266,"added":"2026-05-25 21:38:06.213865+00","description":"Framework from Zhejiang University for building, evaluating, and deploying GUI agents. Features online RL training, standardized benchmarks, and deployment tools. 1.2K stars. Research-backed approach to training agents that interact with graphical interfaces."}
